 */
if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) { exit; }
return array(
array('Agent','agent','Agents','An AI system that takes a goal, breaks it into steps, and carries those steps out using tools, rather than answering a single question and stopping. The defining trait is initiative between instructions: the agent decides what to do next.','A research agent that searches, reads, and compiles a briefing from one request.','Emerged from decades of AI research; the current usage solidified with the 2023-2024 wave of LLM-based agents.'),
array('Agent Handoff','agent-handoff','Agents','Transferring control, context, and accumulated state from one agent to another mid-task. Done well, the receiving agent continues without re-asking; done badly, context is lost at the seam and the user repeats themselves.','A support triage agent passing a billing dispute, with full conversation history, to a specialist billing agent.',''),
array('Agent Memory','agent-memory','Agents','A persistent store that lets an agent recall facts, preferences, and prior work across sessions instead of starting cold each time. Typically split into a short-term working scratchpad and a long-term store, each with different retention and privacy implications.','An assistant that remembers your reporting format from last quarter without being retold.',''),
array('Agent Orchestration','agent-orchestration','Agents','Coordinating multiple agents, tools, and steps toward one goal, including sequencing, retries, and deciding which component handles what. It is the management layer that turns individual capabilities into a working system.','A planner agent assigning research, drafting, and review to three worker agents and assembling the result.',''),
array('Agent Washing','agent-washing','Agents','Marketing a simple scripted workflow as an autonomous agent to ride the trend. The tell is that the "agent" cannot deviate from its script when conditions change.','A vendor rebranding a five-step form automation as "agentic AI" in a sales deck.','Analyst coinage, popularized by Gartner in 2025 vendor-claim critiques.'),
array('Agentic AI','agentic-ai','Agents','AI capable of planning and acting autonomously toward a goal, using tools and adjusting course based on results. The term marks the shift from AI that answers to AI that does, which is also the shift that creates most new governance exposure.','A procurement workflow where the AI requests quotes, compares them, and drafts the purchase order.','Industry usage from roughly 2024 onward, as tool-using LLM systems reached production.'),
array('AI Workflow','ai-workflow','Agents','A coordinated, repeatable process in which AI performs defined steps, usually with fixed order and human checkpoints. Distinct from an agent in that the path is designed in advance rather than chosen at run time.','Invoice intake, extraction, validation, and posting running as one automated sequence.',''),
array('Autonomy Level','autonomy-level','Agents','How far an agent may act before a human must confirm, ranging from suggest-only through approve-to-execute to fully autonomous. Setting this level deliberately, per task, is one of the core agent governance decisions.','An agent allowed to draft emails freely but required to get approval before sending.',''),
array('Browser Agent','browser-agent','Agents','An agent that operates a web browser the way a person does: navigating pages, filling forms, clicking, and extracting data. Powerful for research and procurement tasks, and a new category of access that security reviews often have no slot for.','An agent comparing supplier pricing across a dozen vendor portals.',''),
array('Coding Agent','coding-agent','Agents','An agent that reads a repository, edits files, runs tests, and opens pull requests with limited supervision. It compresses development time and simultaneously raises the question of who reviews machine-written changes.','Claude Code fixing a failing test suite and submitting the patch for human review.',''),
array('Computer Use','computer-use','Agents','An agent capability to operate a graphical interface directly, reading the screen and issuing clicks and keystrokes. It extends automation to software that has no API, which is exactly the software with the fewest guardrails.','An agent processing claims inside a legacy desktop application.','Introduced as a named capability by Anthropic in October 2024.'),
array('Function Calling (Tool Use)','function-calling-tool-use','Agents','The mechanism by which a model invokes external tools, APIs, or code through structured requests instead of plain text. It is what connects a language model to real systems, and therefore where read-only assistance becomes action with consequences.','A model calling a weather API, then a calendar API, to reschedule a site visit.','Introduced commercially in OpenAI\'s June 2023 API release; now standard across providers.'),
array('Human in the Loop (HITL)','human-in-the-loop-hitl','Agents','A design that requires human approval at defined checkpoints before an AI action takes effect. The control is only as good as the checkpoint placement: approval fatigue on low-stakes items trains people to rubber-stamp the high-stakes ones.','A manager approving each AI-drafted payment before release.','Borrowed from control-systems and human-factors engineering, decades before LLMs.'),
array('Loop Guard','loop-guard','Agents','A hard limit on iterations, time, or spend that stops a runaway agent loop. Agents that retry failed steps can burn unbounded cost pursuing an impossible goal unless something external ends the attempt.','A cap of 25 steps and $5 of inference per task, after which the agent stops and reports.',''),
array('Multi-Agent System','multi-agent-system','Agents','Several specialized agents collaborating, delegating, or debating to solve a task no single agent handles well. The architecture improves quality and adds coordination failure modes that single-agent systems do not have.','A researcher agent, a critic agent, and a writer agent producing a due-diligence memo.','A named research field since the 1990s; revived in LLM form from 2023.'),
array('Orchestrator-Worker Pattern','orchestrator-worker-pattern','Agents','A lead agent decomposes a task and delegates subtasks to subordinate agents, then assembles their outputs. The pattern behind most production "deep research" systems, and the reason one user request can fan out into dozens of model calls.','A lead agent splitting a market analysis into five parallel research threads.',''),
array('Planner','planner','Agents','The component that decomposes a goal into an ordered set of steps before execution begins. Plan quality bounds agent quality: a flawless executor of a bad plan still fails.','A task graph turning "prepare the board pack" into gather, draft, chart, and review steps.',''),
array('Prompt Chaining','prompt-chaining','Agents','Connecting prompts in sequence so each step\'s output feeds the next step\'s input. The predecessor of full agents, still the right tool when the path is known in advance.','Extract key figures, then summarize them, then format the summary as an email, as three chained calls.',''),
array('Scratchpad','scratchpad','Agents','A working area where a model writes intermediate reasoning, notes, or plans that inform its final answer but are not the answer. Inspecting it is often the fastest way to see why an agent did what it did.','A coding agent\'s plan file listing which modules it intends to touch and why.',''),
array('Subagent','subagent','Agents','A scoped agent spawned to handle one subtask and report back, then terminate. Isolation is the point: the subagent gets only the context and permissions its slice of work requires.','A subagent given read access to one folder to summarize its contents, and nothing else.',''),
array('Tool Registry','tool-registry','Agents','The catalog of tools, with their schemas and permissions, that an agent is allowed to call. It is the practical control surface for agent blast radius: an agent cannot misuse a tool it was never granted.','A registry granting the finance agent report-generation tools but not payment execution.',''),
array('Adversarial Testing','adversarial-testing','AI Security & Assurance','Deliberately attacking your own AI system to find what breaks before someone else does. It goes beyond functional QA: the tester behaves like an adversary, probing injection paths, boundary conditions, and output handling rather than confirming the happy path works.','Running injection, boundary, and output tests against a customer-facing chatbot before launch.',''),
array('Agent Boundary','agent-boundary','AI Security & Assurance','The documented limit on what an agent may read, write, and trigger. Writing boundaries down is the control: an undocumented boundary cannot be audited, and in a boundary matrix the empty cells are findings, not omissions.','A grid showing each agent\'s permitted data sources, write targets, and downstream actions, with every blank cell explained.',''),
array('AI System Plan','ai-system-plan','AI Security & Assurance','Documentation of an AI system\'s purpose, controls, and monitoring, in the format NIST SP 800-18r2 defines. It extends the long-standing system security plan discipline to AI, giving assessors one place to see what the system does and how it is protected.','An SSP-style document covering a deployed RAG system\'s data sources, access controls, and monitoring.','NIST SP 800-18 Revision 2, which extended system security planning to AI systems.'),
array('AIVSS (AI Vulnerability Scoring System)','aivss-ai-vulnerability-scoring-system','AI Security & Assurance','An OWASP scoring method for rating the severity of AI-specific vulnerabilities, the AI analog of CVSS for conventional software flaws. Scores are what turn a pile of findings into a sequenced remediation roadmap.','Ranking a prompt-injection exposure against a model-exfiltration risk to decide which gets fixed first.','OWASP AI Vulnerability Scoring System project.'),
array('Annex I / Annex III (EU AI Act)','annex-i-annex-iii-eu-ai-act','AI Security & Assurance','The two routes into high-risk classification under the EU AI Act: Annex I covers AI embedded in already-regulated products, Annex III lists stand-alone high-risk use cases such as hiring and credit. Which annex applies decides the obligation set and the compliance deadline.','An AI hiring screener landing in Annex III and inheriting the full high-risk obligation stack.','EU AI Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689; deadlines amended by the 2026 Digital Omnibus.'),
array('Attack Surface','attack-surface','AI Security & Assurance','Every point where an attacker can attempt to reach or influence a system. AI expands it in kind, not just degree: inference endpoints, prompt channels, retrieval sources, and tool calls are all new entry points the pre-AI threat model never listed.','An inventory that adds the chatbot\'s prompt box and its retrieval store to the classic network and application entries.','Long-standing security-engineering concept, predating AI.'),
array('Audit Trail','audit-trail','AI Security & Assurance','A tamper-resistant record of who did what, when, and under what authority. Agent actions belong in it exactly as human actions do; an agent that acts outside the logged record is an agent that cannot be investigated.','A log entry showing which agent approved a refund, under which delegation, at what time.',''),
array('Blast Radius','blast-radius','AI Security & Assurance','How much damage a compromised identity or agent can cause before anything stops it. Read access leaks data; write access changes systems, which is why write permissions are what make a blast radius large.','Measuring what a hijacked procurement agent could actually order, cancel, or pay before a control intervenes.','Borrowed from site-reliability engineering; applied to AI agents from roughly 2024.'),
array('CE Marking','ce-marking','AI Security & Assurance','A manufacturer\'s declaration that a product meets EU requirements and may be sold in the single market. It is a statement of product compliance, not a security assurance: a CE mark says the conformity process ran, not that the system resists attack.','An AI-enabled medical device carrying a CE mark while still needing its own security assessment.','EU product-conformity regime, extended to AI by the EU AI Act.'),
array('Compensating Control','compensating-control','AI Security & Assurance','A substitute control applied when the preferred control cannot be deployed in time. It buys risk reduction now at the cost of tracking debt: every compensating control carries an implicit promise to install the real one.','A WAF rule blocking a known exploit pattern while the underlying patch waits for a maintenance window.','Standard audit and compliance vocabulary, notably from PCI DSS.'),
array('Conformity Assessment','conformity-assessment','AI Security & Assurance','The formal process of demonstrating a product meets regulatory requirements before it goes to market. Depending on classification it is self-assessed or third-party assessed, and the difference determines cost, timeline, and who signs.','A high-risk AI system routed through a notified body instead of a self-declaration.','EU product-safety law; central to the EU AI Act\'s high-risk regime.'),
array('Context Isolation','context-isolation','AI Security & Assurance','Keeping one user\'s prompts, retrieved data, and cached results out of another user\'s session. Failures here are leaks with no attacker involved: the system volunteers one tenant\'s data to another through shared context or cache.','A multi-tenant assistant that never lets tenant A\'s retrieved documents surface in tenant B\'s answers.',''),
array('COSAiS (Control Overlays for Securing AI Systems)','cosais-control-overlays-for-securing-ai-systems','AI Security & Assurance','A NIST project mapping the SP 800-53 control catalog onto AI systems. It is the implementation detail beneath the Cyber AI Profile: where the profile says what outcomes matter, the overlays say which controls produce them.','Selecting the overlay controls for a generative AI deployment instead of hand-picking from 800-53.','NIST Control Overlays for Securing AI Systems project.'),
array('Cyber AI Profile (NIST IR 8596)','cyber-ai-profile-nist-ir-8596','AI Security & Assurance','A NIST profile applying the Cybersecurity Framework 2.0 to AI, organized around securing AI systems, defending with AI, and thwarting AI-enabled attacks. It bridges CSF 2.0 and the AI RMF so security teams do not need two disconnected frameworks.','Mapping an existing CSF 2.0 program onto AI systems using the profile\'s Secure, Defend, and Thwart lenses.','NIST IR 8596.'),
array('Cyber Resilience Act (CRA)','cyber-resilience-act-cra','AI Security & Assurance','An EU regulation setting lifecycle cybersecurity requirements for products with digital elements, from secure development through vulnerability handling and updates. Its Article 12(1) deems CRA compliance to satisfy part of AI Act Article 15, tying the two regimes together.','A software vendor\'s CRA conformity work counting toward its AI Act cybersecurity obligations.','EU Cyber Resilience Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/2847.'),
array('Data Loss Prevention (DLP)','data-loss-prevention-dlp','AI Security & Assurance','Controls that detect and block sensitive data leaving the organization. Classic DLP watches email, uploads, and endpoints; it is rarely tuned to watch a prompt box, which is now one of the busiest exfiltration channels in the building.','Extending DLP policies to inspect what employees paste into public AI tools.','Established security control category; AI-channel coverage is the current gap.'),
array('Data Provenance','data-provenance','AI Security & Assurance','A verified record of where data came from and what it may be used for. Consent, licensing, and residency obligations travel with the data into every model that touches it, so provenance is what makes a training set defensible rather than merely available.','Tracing a fine-tuning dataset back to its licensed sources before a customer audit asks.',''),
array('Defensible Evidence','defensible-evidence','AI Security & Assurance','A dated, owned artifact that answers what the organization knew and when it knew it. Assurance is an opinion; evidence is a document, and a regulator or plaintiff accepts only the second.','A signed risk assessment with a date and an owner, produced in response to a regulator\'s request.',''),
array('Digital Omnibus (AI)','digital-omnibus-ai','AI Security & Assurance','The 2026 package of targeted amendments to the EU AI Act, deferring high-risk deadlines and restructuring conformity assessment. Its practical effect is calendar relief, not obligation relief: Annex III high-risk duties moved to December 2027 while transparency dates held.','Replanning an AI Act compliance roadmap around the deferred Annex III date instead of the original 2026 deadline.','EU Digital Omnibus package, 2026.'),
array('DPIA (Data Protection Impact Assessment)','dpia-data-protection-impact-assessment','AI Security & Assurance','A documented assessment of privacy risk required before certain high-risk processing. Many AI deployments trigger the duty because they process personal data in new ways at scale, and the DPIA is often the first document a supervisory authority requests.','Completing a DPIA before deploying an AI system that screens customer communications.','GDPR Article 35.'),
array('Harmonised Standard','harmonised-standard','AI Security & Assurance','A European standard that, once cited in the Official Journal, gives a presumption of conformity with the regulation it supports. Following the standard becomes the practical route to compliance because it shifts the burden of proof onto anyone claiming otherwise.','Building an AI quality-management system against the harmonised standard instead of arguing conformity from first principles.','EU standardisation system under Regulation (EU) 1025/2012.'),
array('Incident Response (IR)','incident-response-ir','AI Security & Assurance','The documented and rehearsed process for detecting, containing, and recovering from a security event. The rehearsal is the substance: an untested plan is treated as no plan, because the first live incident is the worst possible rehearsal.','A tabletop exercise walking the team through a prompt-injection incident before one happens.','Codified in NIST SP 800-61.'),
array('Machine Identity','machine-identity','AI Security & Assurance','Any credential belonging to software rather than a person: service accounts, API keys, certificates, tokens. They now outnumber human identities in most environments, and each new agent adds several more.','An inventory pass that finds five machine credentials for every employee login.',''),
array('Materiality','materiality','AI Security & Assurance','Whether an event is significant enough to require disclosure to investors or regulators. For US public companies a materiality determination on a cyber incident starts the SEC\'s four-business-day disclosure clock, which makes the determination itself a governed process.','A materiality assessment convened within hours of discovering a breach involving an AI system.','SEC cybersecurity disclosure rules, 2023.'),
array('MITRE ATLAS','mitre-atlas','AI Security & Assurance','A public knowledge base of observed adversary tactics and techniques against AI systems, the ATT&CK equivalent for AI. It turns AI threat modeling from speculation into pattern-matching against documented attacks.','Mapping a deployed model\'s exposures against ATLAS techniques during a threat-modeling session.','MITRE ATLAS, launched 2021.'),
array('Model Artifact','model-artifact','AI Security & Assurance','The weights, adapters, and tuning data that constitute a trained model. It is a production asset with recovery requirements: losing it can mean losing a capability no backup of the surrounding code can restore.','Including model weights and adapters in the disaster-recovery inventory with defined restore objectives.',''),
array('Model Exfiltration','model-exfiltration','AI Security & Assurance','Extracting a model\'s behavior or training data through repeated queries. Each request looks legitimate on its own; the theft only appears in the aggregate pattern, which is why per-request controls miss it.','Rate and pattern monitoring that flags a customer account systematically mapping a model\'s decision boundary.',''),
array('Model Risk Management (MRM)','model-risk-management-mrm','AI Security & Assurance','Supervisory expectations for validating and governing models used in regulated decisions: independent validation, ongoing monitoring, and documented limitations. SR 26-2 and OCC 2026-13 replaced the long-standing SR 11-7 in April 2026, extending the discipline explicitly to AI and machine learning models.','A bank\'s validation team independently testing an AI credit model before it touches a lending decision.','Federal Reserve SR 26-2 and OCC Bulletin 2026-13, April 2026, superseding SR 11-7.'),
array('Model Supply Chain','model-supply-chain','AI Security & Assurance','Everything a model depends on that the organization did not build: base weights, tuning datasets, training pipelines, and the services that host them. Each inherited component carries inherited risk that procurement never priced.','A register listing the base model, dataset sources, and pipeline dependencies behind each deployed AI system.',''),
array('NIST SP 800-207','nist-sp-800-207','AI Security & Assurance','The NIST publication defining zero trust architecture and its tenets: verify every request, assume breach, grant least privilege. It was written before agent traffic existed, so applying it to AI means extending its identity and policy model to non-human actors it never anticipated.','Using 800-207 tenets to design per-request authorization for agent tool calls.','NIST SP 800-207, published 2020.'),
array('Non-Human Identity (NHI)','non-human-identity-nhi','AI Security & Assurance','Any identity that can authenticate and act without a person present: service accounts, workload identities, and now AI agents. It is the population most access reviews miss, because review processes were designed around employees.','An access-review cycle that includes agent credentials with the same rigor as user accounts.',''),
array('Notified Body','notified-body','AI Security & Assurance','An accredited organization designated to carry out third-party conformity assessment under EU product law. For the AI Act\'s high-risk systems, notified-body capacity is the current constraint: obligations can arrive faster than assessors can be accredited.','Booking a notified-body assessment slot months ahead of a high-risk system\'s market date.','EU conformity-assessment regime; designated per regulation including the AI Act.'),
array('Output Filtering','output-filtering','AI Security & Assurance','Inspecting generated responses before release and blocking or redacting what should not go out. It is the last line: it catches what retrieval pulled in, what the prompt coaxed out, and what upstream controls missed.','A filter redacting account numbers from a support bot\'s answers regardless of how they entered the context.',''),
array('OWASP LLM Top 10','owasp-llm-top-10','AI Security & Assurance','The consensus list of the highest-priority security risks in LLM applications, from prompt injection through unbounded consumption. It functions as the scoring baseline for AI application security the way the original OWASP Top 10 does for web.','Structuring an AI application security review as a walk through the ten categories.','OWASP, first released 2023.'),
array('Permission-Based Execution','permission-based-execution','AI Security & Assurance','Evaluating each attempted action against policy at the moment it is attempted, rather than trusting a role granted in advance. It is enforcement, not documentation: the policy engine sits in the execution path and can say no.','An agent\'s payment attempt checked against amount and counterparty policy at call time.',''),
array('Presumption of Conformity','presumption-of-conformity','AI Security & Assurance','The legal assumption that following a cited standard satisfies the underlying regulatory requirement. It shifts the burden of proof: a challenger must show the standard was not followed or does not cover the case, rather than the deployer proving compliance from scratch.','Citing conformity with a harmonised standard as the front-line answer to an enforcement inquiry.','EU product-safety law doctrine.'),
array('Privacy Budget','privacy-budget','AI Security & Assurance','The parameter, epsilon, bounding how much any single record can influence a model\'s output under differential privacy. The number is the claim: a "differentially private" system quoted without an epsilon value is an unevidenced assertion.','A vendor asked to state the epsilon behind its privacy-preserving analytics claim.','Differential privacy literature, Dwork et al., 2006.'),
array('Right of Erasure','right-of-erasure','AI Security & Assurance','An individual\'s right to have their personal data deleted. In AI systems the practical question is where deletion stops: source rows can be removed while derived embeddings and trained weights still carry the influence, and erasure that stops before the embedding store is incomplete by design.','A deletion workflow that removes the source record and the embeddings generated from it.','GDPR Article 17.'),
array('SBOM (Software Bill of Materials)','sbom-software-bill-of-materials','AI Security & Assurance','An inventory of the components and dependencies inside a piece of software. It answers component provenance, not data licensing: an SBOM tells you which libraries shipped, and says nothing about what trained the model beside them.','Requiring an SBOM from an AI vendor while separately demanding training-data licensing terms.','Standardized formats SPDX and CycloneDX; mandated in US federal procurement by EO 14028.'),
array('Service Principal','service-principal','AI Security & Assurance','A non-human identity used by an application to authenticate to a service. Its behavior is predictable, which is exactly what distinguishes it from an agent: a service principal does the same thing every night, an agent decides what to do next.','Baselining a service principal\'s fixed access pattern so deviations alert immediately.','Cloud identity-platform vocabulary, notably Microsoft Entra.'),
array('SIEM (Security Information and Event Management)','siem-security-information-and-event-management','AI Security & Assurance','The platform that centralizes logs and correlates them into alerts. Its blind spot is whatever never reaches it, and AI gateway logs often never do, leaving the busiest new traffic channel invisible to the team paid to watch.','Routing AI gateway and agent-action logs into the SIEM alongside firewall and endpoint feeds.','Established security operations category.'),
array('Silent Upgrade','silent-upgrade','AI Security & Assurance','A vendor switching on an AI feature inside software you already run, with no new contract and no procurement event. It is found in release notes, not purchase orders, which is why AI inventories built from contracts alone undercount what is actually running.','A quarterly release-note review that catches a CRM enabling AI summarization by default.',''),
array('SOC 2','soc-2','AI Security & Assurance','An attestation report on a service organization\'s controls over security, availability, and confidentiality, issued by an independent auditor. It is the report enterprise buyers ask for, and its scope section is where AI services quietly fall inside or outside the attestation.','Reading a vendor\'s SOC 2 scope to confirm the AI feature actually sits within the audited boundary.','AICPA Trust Services Criteria.'),
array('Software Provenance','software-provenance','AI Security & Assurance','A verified record of where code, containers, and model weights originated, signed and traceable to a source. It is what lets a deployer distinguish the artifact the vendor built from an artifact something substituted along the way.','Verifying a model file\'s signature against the publisher\'s key before loading it into production.','Supply-chain security practice; frameworks include SLSA and Sigstore.'),
array('Threat Modeling','threat-modeling','AI Security & Assurance','Structured analysis of how a system could be attacked, done before it ships. AI adds questions the old model never asked: what can the prompt channel deliver, what can retrieval import, what can a tool call reach.','A design review that models prompt injection and retrieval poisoning alongside classic network threats.','Established security-engineering practice; methods include STRIDE, from Microsoft.'),
array('Three Lines Model','three-lines-model','AI Security & Assurance','The IIA framework separating risk ownership (first line), oversight (second line), and independent assurance (third line). AI governance sits in the second line: it sets policy and monitors, while the teams deploying AI own the risk and internal audit independently checks both.','Assigning AI policy to risk, AI deployment risk to the business, and AI assurance to internal audit.','Institute of Internal Auditors, Three Lines Model, 2020 revision.'),
array('Tool Allowlisting','tool-allowlisting','AI Security & Assurance','Restricting an agent to a defined set of tools evaluated at execution time. Scope it per workflow, not per agent: the same agent doing two jobs should hold two different tool sets, each as small as the job allows.','A reporting workflow granting read-only tools while the same agent\'s filing workflow adds one write tool.',''),
array('Unbounded Consumption','unbounded-consumption','AI Security & Assurance','Runaway inference volume that imposes cost and exhausts capacity, whether from attack, defect, or an agent loop. It is OWASP LLM10, and in practice it is seen first on an invoice rather than in a dashboard.','A spend alert catching an integration retrying a failing model call thousands of times overnight.','OWASP LLM Top 10, category LLM10.'),
array('Workload Identity','workload-identity','AI Security & Assurance','An identity assigned to a running workload rather than to a person or an application registration, common in cloud and container platforms. It narrows credentials to the workload\'s lifetime, which is the right shape for agent processes that spin up and vanish.','A containerized agent authenticating through its workload identity instead of a shared API key.','Cloud-native identity practice; implementations include SPIFFE and cloud provider workload identity federation.'),
array('Zero Trust','zero-trust','AI Security & Assurance','A security model that verifies every request rather than trusting network location. NIST SP 800-207 defines it, and it is rarely extended to agents: the architecture that never trusts a laptop still routinely trusts whatever an agent asks for once it is inside.','Applying per-request verification to agent tool calls with the same rigor as user requests.','Term popularized by Forrester, 2010; codified in NIST SP 800-207, 2020.'),
array('Activation Function','activation-function','Architecture','A nonlinear function applied to neuron outputs so the network can represent relationships more complex than straight lines. Without nonlinearity, stacking layers adds nothing a single layer could not do.','ReLU, GELU, and SwiGLU are the common choices in modern models.',''),
array('Attention Mechanism','attention-mechanism','Architecture','The component that weights the relevance of each input element when producing each output element, letting a model focus on what matters wherever it sits in the sequence. It is the core of the transformer and the reason context length costs compute.','A translation model attending to the right source word regardless of word order.','Introduced in Bahdanau et al., 2014; made central by the 2017 transformer paper.'),
array('Autoencoder','autoencoder','Architecture','A neural network that learns efficient encodings of unlabeled data by compressing it through an encoder and reconstructing it through a decoder. What survives the squeeze is, by construction, the structure the data actually contains.','Dimensionality reduction and image denoising pipelines.',''),
array('Autoregressive Model','autoregressive-model','Architecture','A model that generates each output conditioned on everything it has generated so far. Token-by-token generation is why LLM output streams, and why an early wrong turn can compound through the rest of an answer.','A chat model producing a sentence one token at a time, each chosen in light of the last.',''),
array('CLIP','clip','Architecture','A model trained to align image and text embeddings in one shared space, so pictures and descriptions of the same thing land near each other. That alignment is what makes zero-shot image classification and text-to-image retrieval work.','Finding product photos from a text query with no task-specific training.','OpenAI, 2021, "Learning Transferable Visual Models From Natural Language Supervision."'),
array('Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)','convolutional-neural-network-cnn','Architecture','A deep learning architecture that processes visual data by sliding learned filters across an image, detecting edges, textures, and shapes at increasing levels of abstraction. It dominated computer vision for a decade and still runs much of production imaging.','Image classification and defect detection on a production line.','LeCun et al., 1989; popularized at scale by AlexNet, 2012.'),
array('Cross-Attention','cross-attention','Architecture','Attention where the queries come from one sequence and the keys and values from another, letting one stream consult a second. It is how a decoder reads an encoder, and how an image generator reads a text prompt.','A text prompt steering an image diffusion model through cross-attention layers.',''),
array('Decoder','decoder','Architecture','The component that generates output tokens one at a time from a representation and the tokens produced so far. GPT-style chat models are decoder-only: the same stack reads the prompt and writes the answer.','A decoder-only model completing text without a separate encoder stage.',''),
array('Dense Model','dense-model','Architecture','A model that activates all of its parameters for every token processed. Simpler to train and serve than sparse alternatives, at the price of spending full compute on every token whether the token needs it or not.','Classic transformer LLMs where each forward pass uses the whole network.',''),
array('Diffusion Model','diffusion-model','Architecture','A class of generative models that create data by learning to reverse a noising process, iteratively removing noise until an image, video, or audio sample emerges. Quality comes from many small denoising steps rather than one leap.','Stable Diffusion and Midjourney generating images from text prompts.','Ho et al., 2020, "Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Models."'),
array('Diffusion Transformer (DiT)','diffusion-transformer-dit','Architecture','A diffusion model that replaces the U-Net backbone with a transformer, bringing transformer scaling behavior to image and video generation. Most modern large media generators build on this design.','Video generation models scaling quality by scaling the transformer backbone.','Peebles and Xie, 2023, "Scalable Diffusion Models with Transformers."'),
array('Encoder','encoder','Architecture','The component that converts input into a dense representation the rest of the system can use. Encoder-only models excel at understanding tasks, classification, retrieval, and similarity, where nothing needs to be generated.','BERT-style models embedding sentences for search.',''),
array('Encoder-Decoder','encoder-decoder','Architecture','An architecture pairing an encoder for the input with a decoder for the output, the natural shape for tasks that transform one sequence into another. Translation and summarization were its home ground before decoder-only models absorbed most tasks.','T5 translating or summarizing by encoding the source and decoding the target.',''),
array('Feed-Forward Network (FFN)','feed-forward-network-ffn','Architecture','The position-wise dense layers inside each transformer block, applied to every token independently between attention steps. Much of what a model knows, its stored factual associations, lives in these layers.','Interpretability work locating factual recall in FFN weights.',''),
array('Flash Attention','flash-attention','Architecture','A memory-efficient attention implementation that restructures the computation to minimize reads and writes to GPU memory. Same mathematics, dramatically better hardware behavior, which is what made today\'s long context windows affordable.','Serving a long-context model at a fraction of the memory cost of naive attention.','Dao et al., 2022, "FlashAttention."'),
array('Generative Adversarial Network (GAN)','generative-adversarial-network-gan','Architecture','An architecture in which two networks compete: a generator creates synthetic data and a discriminator judges real from fake, each improving against the other. The adversarial game produced the first convincingly realistic synthetic faces.','Style transfer, super-resolution, and early deepfake generation.','Goodfellow et al., 2014.'),
array('Grounding','grounding','Architecture','Anchoring a model\'s responses to trusted sources rather than its parametric memory. A grounded answer can cite where it came from; an ungrounded one can only assert.','A RAG system answering from retrieved policy documents and citing them.',''),
array('Knowledge Graph','knowledge-graph','Architecture','A connected representation of entities and their relationships, storing facts as a network rather than rows. Paired with LLMs it supplies the precise, multi-hop structure that flat text retrieval loses.','An enterprise graph linking customers, contracts, and obligations for exact traversal.',''),
array('Large Language Model (LLM)','large-language-model-llm','Architecture','A generative model trained on vast text corpora, capable of understanding, summarizing, generating, and predicting language. Scale is the operative word: capabilities appear at sizes where the model has absorbed a meaningful fraction of written human knowledge.','GPT-4o, Llama 3, and Claude handling drafting, analysis, and coding tasks.',''),
array('Latent Space','latent-space','Architecture','The compressed internal representation space where a model organizes what it has learned, with similar concepts sitting close together. Movement through this space is meaningful: interpolating between two points produces coherent blends.','Morphing between two faces by walking the latent space between them.',''),
array('Layer Normalization','layer-normalization','Architecture','A technique that normalizes activations within a layer to stabilize and speed training. Deep networks drift without it; pre-norm placement is one reason very deep transformers train reliably.','Pre-norm transformer blocks in most modern LLMs.','Ba et al., 2016.'),
array('Logits','logits','Architecture','The raw, unnormalized scores a model produces before they are converted to probabilities. They are the model\'s opinion in its most honest form, inspected for confidence and manipulated for steering.','Reading logits to measure how certain a classifier really was.',''),
array('LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory)','lstm-long-short-term-memory','Architecture','A recurrent architecture with gating that lets it retain information across long sequences, solving the vanishing-gradient problem that crippled plain RNNs. It carried speech recognition and translation until transformers displaced it.','Speech recognition and text generation systems of the pre-transformer era.','Hochreiter and Schmidhuber, 1997.'),
array('Mamba','mamba','Architecture','A selective state space model offering long-context processing with linear time complexity, against attention\'s quadratic cost. Hybrid designs pair Mamba layers with transformer layers to get length efficiency without giving up attention\'s strengths.','Hybrid Mamba-transformer models serving very long documents cheaply.','Gu and Dao, 2023.'),
array('MCP (Model Context Protocol)','mcp-model-context-protocol','Architecture','An open standard for connecting AI models to tools and data sources through a common interface, so integrations are built once rather than per-model. It is the plumbing standard of the agent era: an MCP server exposes a capability, and any compliant model can use it.','A company exposing its CRM through one MCP server that every AI assistant can call.','Anthropic, November 2024; subsequently adopted across the industry.'),
array('Mixture of Experts (MoE)','mixture-of-experts-moe','Architecture','An architecture combining multiple specialized sub-networks with a router that decides which experts process each input. It buys large total capacity at modest per-token compute, since only a few experts fire per token.','Mixtral routing each token through two of eight experts.','Shazeer et al., 2017, "Outrageously Large Neural Networks."'),
array('Multi-Head Attention','multi-head-attention','Architecture','Running several attention operations in parallel so the model captures different relationship types simultaneously, one head tracking syntax while another tracks reference. Standard in every transformer block.','Separate heads attending to a pronoun\'s antecedent and its verb at once.','Vaswani et al., 2017.'),
array('Multimodal AI','multimodal-ai','Architecture','Models that process, understand, and generate multiple data types, text, images, audio, video, within one system. The practical effect is that a single interface can read a chart, hear a meeting, and answer in prose. Sometimes shortened to simply multimodal.','GPT-4o and Gemini analyzing an uploaded diagram and discussing it in text.',''),
array('Neural Network (ANN)','neural-network-ann','Architecture','A computing system inspired by biological neural networks, built from interconnected nodes whose connection strengths are learned from data. Every deep learning system, from image classifiers to LLMs, is a neural network at heart.','Feedforward networks underlying all of deep learning.','McCulloch and Pitts, 1943; modern form via backpropagation, 1986.'),
array('Positional Encoding','positional-encoding','Architecture','A method for injecting token-order information into a model that otherwise sees an unordered set. Without it, attention cannot distinguish "dog bites man" from "man bites dog."','Sinusoidal or learned encodings added to token embeddings.','Vaswani et al., 2017.'),
array('Recurrent Neural Network (RNN)','recurrent-neural-network-rnn','Architecture','A network class for sequential data in which connections loop, letting past inputs influence present processing. It defined sequence modeling before attention, and its inability to parallelize training is what transformers fixed.','Time-series forecasting and pre-transformer translation systems.',''),
array('Residual Connection','residual-connection','Architecture','A skip connection that adds a layer\'s input to its output, giving gradients a direct path through deep networks. It is the structural trick that made networks hundreds of layers deep trainable at all.','Standard in every deep architecture since ResNet.','He et al., 2015, "Deep Residual Learning."'),
array('RoPE (Rotary Positional Embedding)','rope-rotary-positional-embedding','Architecture','A positional method that rotates query and key vectors by position-dependent angles, encoding relative position directly into attention. It extrapolates to longer sequences better than fixed encodings, which is why most modern open models use it.','Llama-family models handling contexts longer than trained lengths.','Su et al., 2021, "RoFormer."'),
array('Router (MoE Router)','router-moe-router','Architecture','The component in a mixture-of-experts model that selects which experts process each token. Routing quality determines whether capacity is used or wasted, and load balancing across experts is its persistent engineering problem.','A router spreading tokens evenly so no expert sits idle while another saturates.',''),
array('Self-Attention Mechanism','self-attention-mechanism','Architecture','The transformer component that lets every token weigh its relationship to every other token in the sequence, regardless of distance. It is what gives transformers their grasp of long-range context.','Resolving what "it" refers to across a long paragraph.','Vaswani et al., 2017, "Attention Is All You Need."'),
array('Semantic Search','semantic-search','Architecture','Retrieval based on meaning rather than keyword overlap, implemented by comparing embeddings. It finds the document that answers the question even when the question shares no words with it.','A query for "reducing churn" surfacing a document titled "customer retention playbook."',''),
array('Small Language Model (SLM)','small-language-model-slm','Architecture','A lightweight language model optimized for speed, memory footprint, and edge deployment rather than maximum capability. The trade is deliberate: for bounded tasks, a small model that runs locally beats a frontier model that requires a round trip.','Phi and Gemma-class models running on a laptop for classification tasks.',''),
array('Softmax','softmax','Architecture','The function that converts raw scores into a probability distribution summing to one. It is the final step before a model commits to a next-token choice.','Turning logits into the probabilities that sampling draws from.',''),
array('Sparse Model','sparse-model','Architecture','A model that activates only a subset of its parameters per token, typically through mixture-of-experts routing. Total capacity grows without proportional inference cost, which is how very large models stay servable.','An MoE model with huge total parameters but modest active compute per token.',''),
array('State Space Model (SSM)','state-space-model-ssm','Architecture','A sequence architecture that maintains a running compressed state, scaling linearly with sequence length where attention scales quadratically. The active alternative to attention for very long inputs.','Mamba processing book-length documents at linear cost.',''),
array('Transformer','transformer','Architecture','The deep learning architecture built on self-attention, introduced in 2017, that forms the foundation of modern LLMs. Its decisive property was parallelizable training, which let model scale grow with hardware in a way recurrent architectures never could.','GPT, BERT, Gemini, and Claude are all transformers.','Vaswani et al., 2017, "Attention Is All You Need."'),
array('U-Net','u-net','Architecture','An encoder-decoder network with skip connections between matching resolution levels, preserving fine detail through the compression bottleneck. Built for medical image segmentation, it became the denoising backbone of the first diffusion image generators.','The denoiser inside classic Stable Diffusion.','Ronneberger et al., 2015.'),
array('Variational Autoencoder (VAE)','variational-autoencoder-vae','Architecture','An autoencoder that learns a probabilistic latent distribution rather than fixed codes, making the latent space smooth enough to generate from. In image diffusion systems it handles the compression into and out of latent space.','The latent compression stage in Stable Diffusion pipelines.','Kingma and Welling, 2013.'),
array('Vision Transformer (ViT)','vision-transformer-vit','Architecture','An architecture that applies transformer attention to image patches instead of convolutions, treating a picture as a sequence of tiles. At sufficient data scale it matched then passed CNNs, unifying vision and language under one architecture family.','Image classifiers and the vision encoders inside multimodal models.','Dosovitskiy et al., 2020.'),
array('Vision-Language Model (VLM)','vision-language-model-vlm','Architecture','A multimodal model trained to understand both visual inputs and text, connecting what it sees to what it can say. The bridge that lets a chat model read screenshots, charts, and documents.','CLIP, LLaVA, and GPT-4V-class models describing and reasoning over images.',''),
array('AIME','aime','Benchmarks & Evaluation','A competition mathematics exam repurposed to test advanced multi-step reasoning in models. Its problems resist pattern-matching, which is why reasoning-model releases lead with AIME scores.','A reasoning model reporting its AIME solve rate as a headline capability claim.','American Invitational Mathematics Examination, adopted as an AI benchmark from 2024.'),
array('ARC-AGI','arc-agi','Benchmarks & Evaluation','An abstract reasoning benchmark built from novel visual puzzles that cannot be solved by recalling training data. It is deliberately resistant to memorization, making it one of the few tests that measures generalization rather than recall.','Models scoring far below humans on puzzles a child solves by inspection.','Fran\u00e7ois Chollet, "On the Measure of Intelligence," 2019.'),
array('AUC-ROC','auc-roc','Benchmarks & Evaluation','The area under the receiver operating characteristic curve, a threshold-independent measure of how well a classifier separates classes. It answers "how good is the model overall" before anyone picks an operating point.','Comparing two fraud models without committing to an alert threshold.',''),
array('Benchmark','benchmark','Benchmarks & Evaluation','A standardized test used to compare model performance on a defined task set. Useful for ranking and dangerous for deciding: a benchmark measures the test, and vendors optimize for exactly that.','MMLU scores quoted in every model release announcement.',''),
array('BLEU','bleu','Benchmarks & Evaluation','An n-gram overlap metric for machine translation quality, scoring how much generated text matches reference translations. A legacy NLP metric: cheap, standardized, and known to reward surface overlap rather than meaning.','Scoring a translation system against reference translations in a research paper.','Papineni et al., 2002.'),
array('Capability Elicitation','capability-elicitation','Benchmarks & Evaluation','The effort to draw out a model\'s maximum ability before concluding it cannot do something. It exists to prevent false negatives in safety testing: a model that "cannot" assist with a dangerous task under naive prompting may comply under skilled prompting.','Red-teamers using optimized prompts before certifying a capability absent.','Frontier-lab safety evaluation practice.'),
array('Confusion Matrix','confusion-matrix','Benchmarks & Evaluation','A table of true and false positives and negatives that shows exactly how a classifier errs, not just how often. The off-diagonal cells are where the operational story lives.','Discovering a model\'s errors concentrate in one costly direction.',''),
array('Elo Rating','elo-rating','Benchmarks & Evaluation','A relative skill score derived from pairwise comparisons, imported from chess into model evaluation. It ranks models by human preference in head-to-head matchups rather than absolute test scores.','Arena leaderboards ranking chat models by win rate against each other.','Arpad Elo\'s chess rating system, applied to LLMs by LMSYS from 2023.'),
array('F1 Score','f1-score','Benchmarks & Evaluation','The harmonic mean of precision and recall, a single number balancing the two. Standard for classification tasks where both false alarms and misses matter.','Evaluating an entity-extraction system with one balanced figure.',''),
array('GPQA','gpqa','Benchmarks & Evaluation','Graduate-level science questions designed so that even skilled web search does not yield answers, isolating genuine reasoning from lookup. Its "Google-proof" construction is the point.','Frontier models scored on questions PhDs answer near 70 percent.','Rein et al., 2023, "GPQA: A Graduate-Level Google-Proof Q&A Benchmark."'),
array('Ground Truth','ground-truth','Benchmarks & Evaluation','The verified correct answer used as the reference for scoring. Every real evaluation needs it, and producing it is usually the expensive part: without trusted ground truth, an eval measures agreement, not accuracy.','Subject-matter experts labeling a golden set before an eval run.',''),
array('HELM','helm','Benchmarks & Evaluation','A holistic evaluation framework scoring models across many scenarios and metrics at once, accuracy, robustness, fairness, efficiency, rather than one leaderboard number. Its premise is that no single score describes a model.','Reading a model\'s full HELM profile instead of one headline benchmark.','Stanford CRFM, 2022.'),
array('Human Preference Evaluation','human-preference-evaluation','Benchmarks & Evaluation','Scoring models by having human raters compare outputs and pick the better one. It measures what benchmarks cannot, helpfulness and tone, and inherits every bias of the raters, including a documented preference for confident answers.','Pairwise ratings feeding a reward model during alignment training.',''),
array('HumanEval','humaneval','Benchmarks & Evaluation','A Python coding benchmark scored by unit-test pass rate: the model writes a function, the tests decide. It set the early standard for code capability measurement before larger software-engineering benchmarks arrived.','Reporting pass@1 on HumanEval in a model card.','OpenAI, 2021, "Evaluating Large Language Models Trained on Code."'),
array('LMSYS Chatbot Arena','lmsys-chatbot-arena','Benchmarks & Evaluation','A crowd-sourced evaluation where users chat with two anonymous models and vote for the better answer, producing an Elo ranking from millions of matchups. The closest thing to a live market price for model quality.','Checking Arena rankings the week a new model ships.','LMSYS Org, 2023.'),
array('MMLU','mmlu','Benchmarks & Evaluation','The massive multitask language understanding benchmark: multiple-choice questions across 57 subjects from law to physics. For years the default headline number for model knowledge, now saturating as frontier models cluster near the top.','Model launches quoting MMLU alongside newer, harder benchmarks.','Hendrycks et al., 2020.'),
array('Needle in a Haystack','needle-in-a-haystack','Benchmarks & Evaluation','A long-context test that plants one fact in a large document and asks the model to retrieve it. It validates that an advertised context window actually functions across its full length and at every depth.','A retrieval check at 200 thousand tokens, with the fact buried mid-document.',''),
array('Pass@k','pass-k','Benchmarks & Evaluation','The probability that at least one of k sampled attempts is correct, the standard code-generation metric. Pass@1 measures reliability; pass@10 measures whether the capability exists at all.','A model with modest pass@1 but strong pass@10, usable with retry loops.',''),
array('Perplexity','perplexity','Benchmarks & Evaluation','A measure of how well a model predicts a text sample, lower being better. The classic language-modeling quality metric, still used in training but disconnected from downstream usefulness: a lower-perplexity model is not automatically a better assistant.','Tracking perplexity on a validation set during pre-training.',''),
array('Precision and Recall','precision-and-recall','Benchmarks & Evaluation','Precision is the share of positive predictions that are correct; recall is the share of true cases found. Every detection system trades one against the other, and the right balance is a business decision, not a modeling one.','Tuning a compliance monitor toward recall because misses cost more than false alarms.',''),
array('Regression Test (Prompt)','regression-test-prompt','Benchmarks & Evaluation','Rerunning a fixed prompt suite after any change, model version, prompt edit, retrieval update, to detect quality loss. It guards against the silent regressions that provider model updates routinely introduce.','A nightly suite catching a tone shift after a model version bump.',''),
array('ROUGE','rouge','Benchmarks & Evaluation','An overlap metric for summarization quality, counting shared n-grams between generated and reference summaries. Like BLEU, a legacy metric: standardized, cheap, and blind to whether the summary is actually faithful.','Scoring summarizers in research papers before LLM-as-judge methods.','Lin, 2004.'),
array('SWE Bench','swe-bench','Benchmarks & Evaluation','A software engineering benchmark built from real GitHub issues: the model must produce a patch that passes the repository\'s own tests. It measures end-to-end engineering, not snippet writing, which made it the defining coding-agent benchmark.','Coding agents ranked by percentage of real issues resolved.','Jimenez et al., 2023.'),
array('Acceptable Use Policy (AI AUP)','acceptable-use-policy-ai-aup','Business & Adoption','The policy defining permitted and prohibited employee AI use: which tools, which data, which tasks. It is the baseline governance artifact, and an AUP nobody has read governs nothing.','A one-page policy naming approved tools and the data classes barred from prompts.',''),
array('Acceptance Rate','acceptance-rate','Business & Adoption','The share of AI suggestions users actually keep. It is the leading adoption indicator for assistive tools: a falling acceptance rate says the tool is losing the user\'s trust long before usage numbers drop.','Tracking what fraction of code-completion suggestions developers accept.',''),
array('AI FinOps','ai-finops','Business & Adoption','The discipline of tracking and optimizing AI spend against business value, extending cloud FinOps to inference costs. Its unit is cost per outcome, not cost per token: what matters is what a resolved ticket or drafted contract costs.','A dashboard showing cost per resolved support ticket by model and team.','Extension of the FinOps Foundation discipline to AI workloads.'),
array('AI Literacy','ai-literacy','Business & Adoption','Baseline workforce understanding of AI capability, limits, and policy: what the tools can do, where they fail, and what the rules are. Under the EU AI Act it is now a legal requirement for providers and deployers, not just good practice.','Annual training covering hallucination, data handling, and the approved-tool list.','EU AI Act Article 4, in force since February 2025.'),
array('AI Maturity Model','ai-maturity-model','Business & Adoption','A staged framework rating an organization from ad hoc experimentation to an embedded operating model. Its value is diagnostic honesty: knowing which stage you are actually at determines which investments make sense next.','A readiness assessment placing a firm at stage two of five, with a path to three.',''),
array('AI Washing','ai-washing','Business & Adoption','Overstating the AI content of a product or company to attract customers or capital. It is now an SEC enforcement target: regulators treat inflated AI claims the same as any other material misstatement.','Enforcement actions against firms claiming AI capabilities they did not have.','SEC enforcement actions beginning 2024.'),
array('Automation vs Augmentation','automation-vs-augmentation','Business & Adoption','The distinction between AI replacing a task outright and AI increasing a person\'s output on that task. The line determines role design, headcount planning, and the change-management burden of an initiative.','A decision to augment underwriters rather than automate underwriting.',''),
array('Build vs Buy','build-vs-buy','Business & Adoption','The decision between developing an AI capability in house and licensing a vendor solution. The standard portfolio decision, complicated by AI\'s pace: what only a custom build could do last year ships as a product feature this year.','Choosing a vendor contract-review tool over an internal build after pricing the maintenance.',''),
array('Centaur Model','centaur-model','Business & Adoption','A division of labor where human and AI split work by comparative advantage: machine scale and recall paired with human judgment and accountability. Named for the chess format where human-computer teams beat both grandmasters and engines.','An analyst directing AI research sweeps, then making the recommendation personally.','From advanced chess, popularized by Garry Kasparov in the late 1990s.'),
array('Center of Excellence (CoE)','center-of-excellence-coe','Business & Adoption','A central team setting AI standards, tooling, and enablement while business units execute. The hub-and-spoke operating model that balances consistency against speed, and drifts toward bottleneck when the hub tries to do rather than enable.','A CoE publishing the golden path while product teams build on it.',''),
array('Change Management','change-management','Business & Adoption','The structured approach to shifting behavior, roles, and incentives during AI rollout. It is the actual constraint on ROI: the technology usually works, and the organization around it usually has not changed enough to capture the value.','Redesigning review workflows and incentives alongside the tool deployment.',''),
array('Copilot','copilot','Business & Adoption','An AI assistant integrated directly into existing software, suggesting rather than acting autonomously. The dominant enterprise adoption pattern because it upgrades a workflow without replacing it.','A coding copilot completing functions inside the developer\'s editor.','Popularized by GitHub Copilot, 2021.'),
array('Data Residency','data-residency','Business & Adoption','The requirement that data be stored and processed within a specific jurisdiction. It constrains model and provider choice directly: a capability that only runs in another region is a capability the regulated workload cannot use.','Choosing an EU-region deployment to keep customer data inside the jurisdiction.',''),
array('Deflection Rate','deflection-rate','Business & Adoption','The share of support contacts fully resolved without a human. The core support-AI metric, and one that punishes gaming: deflection that leaves problems unresolved returns as escalation and churn.','A support bot resolving six of ten contacts end to end, measured by no-reopen rates.',''),
array('Digital Labor','digital-labor','Business & Adoption','The framing of AI agents as capacity purchased in units of work rather than software seats. It reshapes budgeting and vendor pricing: you buy resolved tickets or processed claims, not licenses.','A vendor quoting per-resolution pricing instead of per-seat subscriptions.','Emerging vendor pricing model, 2024 onward.'),
array('Enterprise Grounding','enterprise-grounding','Business & Adoption','Connecting a model to internal systems of record so its answers reflect company data rather than general knowledge. It is where most enterprise value sits, and most integration cost.','An assistant answering from the firm\'s own contracts and policies, with citations.',''),
array('Golden Path','golden-path','Business & Adoption','The approved and supported way to build AI applications internally: sanctioned models, patterns, and guardrails packaged for teams. A good golden path reduces shadow AI more effectively than prohibition, because it makes the sanctioned route the easiest route.','A platform team shipping templates that make the compliant architecture the default.','Platform-engineering vocabulary, notably from Spotify.'),
array('Human in the Loop Cost','human-in-the-loop-cost','Business & Adoption','The labor cost of reviewing and correcting AI output. Heavy review erases ROI: an AI that drafts in seconds but requires senior review in hours may cost more than the process it replaced.','A contract pipeline repriced after counting reviewer hours per document.',''),
array('Jagged Frontier','jagged-frontier','Business & Adoption','The uneven capability boundary where AI excels at some tasks and fails at adjacent, seemingly similar ones. It explains inconsistent user experience and why task-level piloting beats intuition for deciding what to deploy.','A model acing complex analysis while fumbling a simple formatting request.','Coined in the 2023 Harvard Business School and BCG field study of consultant AI use.'),
array('Model Sprawl','model-sprawl','Business & Adoption','The uncontrolled proliferation of models and AI tools across an organization, each adopted locally and governed nowhere. It drives cost, duplicates spend, and makes a defensible AI inventory impossible until consolidated.','An audit finding four departments running four overlapping AI subscriptions.',''),
array('Outcome-Based Pricing','outcome-based-pricing','Business & Adoption','Charging per resolved task or achieved result instead of per seat or per token. Vendors adopt it where outcomes are countable, support resolutions, qualified leads, and it shifts performance risk from buyer to vendor.','A support-AI contract billing per ticket the AI fully resolves.',''),
array('Performative Adoption','performative-adoption','Business & Adoption','Announcing AI initiatives without changing workflows, incentives, or decision rights. Activity without outcomes: the press release ships, the operating model does not, and the value never arrives.','An "AI-first" announcement followed by unchanged processes a year later.',''),
array('Pilot Purgatory','pilot-purgatory','Business & Adoption','The condition where AI pilots multiply but none reach production. The dominant enterprise failure mode, usually rooted in pilots designed to demonstrate rather than to integrate.','Twelve proofs of concept, zero production deployments, two years running.',''),
array('Proof of Concept (POC)','proof-of-concept-poc','Business & Adoption','A small, scoped test validating technical feasibility before larger investment. It answers "can this work," which is a different question from "will this work here," the question the pilot must answer next.','A two-week POC confirming extraction accuracy on real documents.',''),
array('Task Decomposition','task-decomposition','Business & Adoption','Breaking a job into constituent tasks to identify which are AI-suitable. The basis of honest adoption planning: jobs are rarely automatable, tasks often are, and the split determines the real opportunity.','Decomposing a paralegal role into twenty tasks and finding eight AI-suitable.',''),
array('Time to Value','time-to-value','Business & Adoption','The elapsed time from project start to measurable business benefit. A key portfolio filter: two projects with equal returns are not equal if one pays back in a quarter and the other in two years.','Prioritizing the document-automation project that shows returns within one quarter.',''),
array('Token Budget','token-budget','Business & Adoption','An allocated spend ceiling on model usage for a team or workload, the FinOps control for AI. Budgets convert open-ended inference cost into a governed resource with an owner.','A monthly token allocation per team, with alerts at 80 percent.',''),
array('Total Cost of Ownership (TCO)','total-cost-of-ownership-tco','Business & Adoption','The full lifetime cost of an AI capability: inference, integration, oversight labor, evaluation, and retraining. Routinely understated because the visible API price is the smallest line.','A TCO model where human review and integration dwarf the model bill.',''),
array('Workflow Redesign','workflow-redesign','Business & Adoption','Rebuilding a process around AI capabilities rather than layering AI onto the existing process. It is where the real gains come from: automating a bad process yields a faster bad process.','Collapsing a five-handoff approval chain once AI handles the assembly steps.',''),
array('Zero Data Retention (ZDR)','zero-data-retention-zdr','Business & Adoption','A vendor commitment not to store prompts or outputs after processing completes. A common enterprise contract term, and one worth verifying against the vendor\'s actual architecture rather than the sales deck.','A ZDR clause negotiated before routing client data through a model API.',''),
array('Algorithm','algorithm','Core Concepts','A set of step-by-step rules or instructions a computer follows to solve a problem or perform a calculation. In machine learning the algorithm is the recipe for learning from data; the model is what the recipe produces.','Gradient descent and decision trees are algorithms; a trained classifier is their output.',''),
array('Anomaly Detection','anomaly-detection','Core Concepts','Identifying data points that deviate materially from expected patterns. It is the workhorse of fraud and intrusion detection precisely because it does not need examples of every attack, only a good model of normal.','A monitoring system flagging a login pattern no employee has ever produced.',''),
array('Artificial General Intelligence (AGI)','artificial-general-intelligence-agi','Core Concepts','Hypothetical AI able to understand, learn, and apply knowledge across any intellectual task at or above human level. The term anchors both investment theses and safety debates, despite no agreed test for when it has arrived.','Lab mission statements and policy debates organized around reaching or governing AGI.','Term popularized by Ben Goertzel and Shane Legg, early 2000s.'),
array('Artificial Intelligence (AI)','artificial-intelligence-ai','Core Concepts','The field of computer science dedicated to creating systems that perform tasks typically requiring human intelligence: understanding language, recognizing patterns, making decisions. The umbrella over machine learning, NLP, and everything else in this glossary.','Machine learning, natural language processing, and computer vision are all AI subfields.','Term coined by John McCarthy for the 1956 Dartmouth workshop.'),
array('Artificial Superintelligence (ASI)','artificial-superintelligence-asi','Core Concepts','A hypothetical form of AI far surpassing human intelligence in every field, including creativity, wisdom, and social skill. It matters less as a forecast than as the scenario that motivates much of long-horizon safety research.','The endpoint scenario debated in existential-risk literature.','Popularized by Nick Bostrom\'s "Superintelligence," 2014.'),
array('Automatic Speech Recognition (ASR)','automatic-speech-recognition-asr','Core Concepts','Converting spoken audio into text. Modern ASR approaches human transcription accuracy in clean conditions, which is what made meeting transcription and voice interfaces routine.','A meeting tool producing a searchable transcript in real time.',''),
array('Bitter Lesson','bitter-lesson','Core Concepts','The argument that general methods leveraging computation beat hand-crafted domain knowledge over time, drawn from seventy years of AI history. It is cited to justify betting on scale over feature engineering, and it has aged well.','Choosing a bigger general model over a hand-tuned domain pipeline.','Rich Sutton, "The Bitter Lesson," 2019.'),
array('Computer Vision (CV)','computer-vision-cv','Core Concepts','The field enabling machines to interpret images and video: detecting objects, reading documents, tracking motion. One of the earliest AI capabilities to reach industrial reliability.','Defect detection on a production line running at camera frame rate.',''),
array('Data Set','data-set','Core Concepts','A structured collection of data used to train, evaluate, and test models. Its composition quietly determines what the model can and cannot do, which makes dataset documentation a governance artifact, not housekeeping.','ImageNet for vision; Common Crawl for language pre-training.',''),
array('Deep Learning (DL)','deep-learning-dl','Core Concepts','A subset of machine learning based on neural networks with many layers, which learn their own representations from raw data rather than relying on hand-built features. It is the engine behind image recognition, speech, and large language models.','A deep network learning edge, texture, and object concepts from pixels alone.',''),
array('Digital Twin','digital-twin','Core Concepts','A live virtual model of a physical asset or process, fed by real data and used for simulation and optimization. It lets an operator test changes in software before risking them in steel.','Simulating a production-line change on the twin before touching the floor.',''),
array('Discriminative AI','discriminative-ai','Core Concepts','Models that classify existing data or predict labels rather than generating new content. The quiet majority of production AI: most deployed models decide, they do not create.','Spam classification and sentiment analysis running billions of times daily.',''),
array('Embodied AI','embodied-ai','Core Concepts','AI operating through a physical body, tied to sensors and actuators, where mistakes have physics. The gap between digital and embodied performance remains one of the field\'s most stubborn frontiers.','Warehouse picking robots handling variable, cluttered objects.',''),
array('Emergent Capability','emergent-capability','Core Concepts','A skill that appears only above a certain model scale and was absent in smaller versions. Emergence is why capability forecasting is hard: the next scale step may unlock abilities nobody planned for.','Multi-step arithmetic appearing abruptly as model size crossed a threshold.','Wei et al., 2022, "Emergent Abilities of Large Language Models."'),
array('Expert System','expert-system','Core Concepts','Early AI that encoded human expert rules into if-then logic for a narrow domain. Its rise and stall carry the field\'s founding lesson: hand-written rules do not scale to the messiness of the real world.','MYCIN recommending antibiotics from encoded clinical rules in the 1970s.','Dominant AI paradigm of the 1970s and 1980s.'),
array('Federated Learning','federated-learning','Core Concepts','Training a shared model across decentralized devices without moving raw data to a central server; only model updates travel. It trades engineering complexity for privacy and residency advantages.','Phone keyboards improving prediction from usage that never leaves the device.','Google, 2016.'),
array('Foundation Model','foundation-model','Core Concepts','A large model trained on broad data at scale that serves as the base for many downstream tasks. The economic point is amortization: one enormous training run, adapted cheaply a thousand ways.','GPT, Claude, and Llama serving as bases for countless products.','Term coined by the Stanford Institute for Human-Centered AI, 2021.'),
array('Frontier Model','frontier-model','Core Concepts','A model at or near the current maximum of capability, typically the largest and most recently released systems. The designation carries regulatory weight: frontier status increasingly triggers evaluation and reporting obligations.','A new flagship release undergoing pre-deployment safety evaluation.',''),
array('Generative AI (GenAI)','generative-ai-genai','Core Concepts','Models that create new content, text, images, video, audio, code, from patterns learned in training data. The 2022 shift from AI that classifies to AI that produces is what put this glossary on your reading list.','ChatGPT, Midjourney, and Claude producing drafts, images, and code on request.',''),
array('Machine Learning (ML)','machine-learning-ml','Core Concepts','The subset of AI focused on systems that learn from data and improve with experience rather than following explicitly programmed rules. Nearly everything called AI in production is machine learning underneath.','A recommendation engine improving as it observes more behavior.','Term coined by Arthur Samuel, 1959.'),
array('Moravec\'s Paradox','moravec-s-paradox','Core Concepts','The observation that abstract reasoning is comparatively easy for machines while sensorimotor skills that feel effortless to humans are hard. It explains why chess fell decades before laundry folding.','Superhuman chess coexisting with clumsy robot manipulation.','Hans Moravec, "Mind Children," 1988.'),
array('Narrow AI (Weak AI)','narrow-ai-weak-ai','Core Concepts','AI designed and trained for a specific task or narrow range of tasks, with no ability to generalize beyond it. Every deployed system today is narrow AI, however broad its marketing.','Spam filters, chess engines, and voice assistants each excelling at one thing.',''),
array('Natural Language Generation (NLG)','natural-language-generation-nlg','Core Concepts','The subfield focused on producing fluent, human-readable text from data or intent. Once template-driven and stilted, now indistinguishable from drafting, which changed both its usefulness and its risks.','Automated earnings summaries generated from financial data.',''),
array('Natural Language Processing (NLP)','natural-language-processing-nlp','Core Concepts','The field covering machine understanding and generation of human language. Its problems, translation, sentiment, summarization, were separate research tracks until large language models absorbed most of them into one capability.','Sentiment analysis, translation, and summarization as classic NLP tasks.',''),
array('Natural Language Understanding (NLU)','natural-language-understanding-nlu','Core Concepts','The subfield focused on extracting meaning and intent from text, as opposed to producing it. It is what turns "I can\'t log in" into an actionable support category.','Intent classification routing tickets in a support system.',''),
array('Neurosymbolic AI','neurosymbolic-ai','Core Concepts','A hybrid approach combining neural networks with symbolic logic and rules: perception from the network, guarantees from the rules. Attractive wherever answers must be both learned and provably compliant.','Neural document extraction feeding a deterministic rules engine for compliance decisions.',''),
array('Optical Character Recognition (OCR)','optical-character-recognition-ocr','Core Concepts','Extracting machine-readable text from images or scanned documents. Decades old, newly relevant: OCR is the front door through which paper enters every AI document pipeline.','Digitizing invoices before an extraction model reads them.',''),
array('Predictive AI','predictive-ai','Core Concepts','AI that forecasts outcomes from historical data rather than generating content. It ran the enterprise quietly for a decade before generative AI took the spotlight, and it still makes most of the money.','Churn and demand forecasting driving retention and inventory decisions.',''),
array('Reasoning Model','reasoning-model','Core Concepts','A model optimized to work through multi-step problems before answering, spending extra inference compute on deliberate chains of reasoning. The design trade is latency and cost for accuracy on hard problems.','A reasoning model taking thirty seconds on a proof a chat model fumbles instantly.','Class established by OpenAI\'s o1, September 2024.'),
array('Recommender System','recommender-system','Core Concepts','A model that ranks and suggests items based on user behavior and item features. The most economically consequential AI most people touch daily without naming it.','Streaming and e-commerce suggestions driving a large share of consumption.',''),
array('Reinforcement Learning (RL)','reinforcement-learning-rl','Core Concepts','A paradigm in which an agent learns by taking actions in an environment and receiving rewards or penalties, improving through trial and error rather than labeled examples. It trained game champions first and now post-trains reasoning models.','Game-playing agents, robotics, and the RL stage of modern model training.',''),
array('Scaling Laws','scaling-laws','Core Concepts','Empirical relationships showing predictable capability gains as compute, data, and parameters increase. They turned model development from craft into capital planning: labs buy capability on a curve.','Sizing a training run from the curves before committing the budget.','Kaplan et al., 2020; refined by the Chinchilla paper, 2022.'),
array('Self-Supervised Learning','self-supervised-learning','Core Concepts','Training in which the model creates its own labels from the data, such as predicting the next token or a masked word. It unlocked web-scale training by removing the human labeling bottleneck, and it is how LLMs are pre-trained.','Next-token prediction over trillions of words, no annotators required.',''),
array('Semi-Supervised Learning','semi-supervised-learning','Core Concepts','Training on a small labeled set combined with a large unlabeled set, letting scarce annotation stretch across abundant data. The practical middle path when labels are expensive and data is not.','Labeling one percent of records and propagating structure to the rest.',''),
array('Supervised Learning','supervised-learning','Core Concepts','Training on labeled input-output pairs so the model learns to predict the label for new inputs. The classic paradigm behind most production classifiers and forecasters.','Spam-or-not-spam classification learned from labeled email.',''),
array('Symbolic AI','symbolic-ai','Core Concepts','Rule-based AI that manipulates explicit symbols and logic rather than learning statistical patterns. The field\'s first paradigm, and the source of properties neural methods still lack: transparency and guarantees.','Expert systems of the 1980s encoding knowledge as rules.',''),
array('Text to Speech (TTS)','text-to-speech-tts','Core Concepts','Converting text into synthetic spoken audio. Modern TTS crossed the naturalness threshold where listeners stop noticing, which enabled voice assistants and also voice-cloning fraud.','Audiobook narration generated at production quality.',''),
array('Transfer Learning','transfer-learning','Core Concepts','Reusing a model trained on one task as the starting point for another, carrying learned representations across. It is why a modest dataset can now produce a strong specialized model: most of the learning happened before you arrived.','Fine-tuning a general image model for defect detection with a few thousand examples.',''),
array('Turing Test','turing-test','Core Concepts','A test of whether a machine\'s conversational behavior is indistinguishable from a human\'s. Historically the field\'s north star, now largely superseded: modern models pass casual versions while the interesting capability questions have moved elsewhere.','Chatbots passing short conversational judgments that Turing proposed in 1950.','Alan Turing, "Computing Machinery and Intelligence," 1950.'),
array('Unsupervised Learning','unsupervised-learning','Core Concepts','Learning structure from unlabeled data: clusters, patterns, and groupings no one specified in advance. It finds the categories; humans decide what they mean.','Customer segmentation discovered through clustering rather than assumption.',''),
array('World Model','world-model','Core Concepts','An internal learned representation of how an environment behaves, supporting prediction and planning. Whether large models form genuine world models or surface statistics is one of the field\'s live arguments.','Video models that simulate plausible physics when generating motion.',''),
array('Beam Search','beam-search','Prompting & Interaction','A decoding strategy that keeps several candidate sequences alive and expands the most promising, rather than committing to one token at a time. Common in translation, where the best sentence is not always built from the best next word.','A translation system tracking five candidate renderings before choosing.',''),
array('Chain-of-Thought (CoT)','chain-of-thought-cot','Prompting & Interaction','A prompting technique that encourages the model to generate intermediate reasoning steps before the final answer. Making the reasoning explicit improves accuracy on multi-step problems and gives reviewers something to inspect when the answer is wrong.','Adding "think step by step" and watching arithmetic accuracy jump.','Wei et al., 2022, "Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning."'),
array('Citation / Attribution','citation-attribution','Prompting & Interaction','Linking generated claims back to the source documents that support them. Required in regulated reporting and increasingly expected everywhere: an answer that cites can be checked, an answer that does not must be trusted.','A research assistant footnoting each claim to a retrieved document.',''),
array('Constrained Decoding','constrained-decoding','Prompting & Interaction','Restricting token choices at generation time so output must satisfy a grammar or schema. It converts "usually valid" into "guaranteed valid," which is the difference between a demo and an integration.','Function arguments generated under a JSON grammar that cannot produce invalid syntax.',''),
array('Context Rot','context-rot','Prompting & Interaction','Quality decay as a conversation or working context grows long and noisy: the model starts missing instructions it followed an hour ago. Fixed by summarizing state and restarting clean rather than pushing on.','A long session drifting off format until a fresh thread restores it.',''),
array('Context Stuffing','context-stuffing','Prompting & Interaction','Filling the context window with as much reference material as possible on the theory that more is better. It often degrades precision: relevance beats volume, and retrieval that selects usually outperforms context that hoards.','Pasting nine documents when the two relevant ones would score higher.',''),
array('Context Window','context-window','Prompting & Interaction','The maximum number of tokens a model can process and retain during a single interaction: its working memory. Everything the model should consider, instructions, documents, history, must fit inside it.','A 200 thousand token window holding an entire contract set for review.',''),
array('Delimiters','delimiters','Prompting & Interaction','Markers that separate instructions from data inside a prompt, XML tags, triple backticks, headers. They reduce the chance the model treats quoted content as commands, which is also the first cheap defense against injection.','Wrapping a pasted email in tags so its text is analyzed, not obeyed.',''),
array('Few-Shot Prompting','few-shot-prompting','Prompting & Interaction','Providing a few in-context examples that demonstrate the desired output format or task handling. The examples do the teaching: format, tone, and edge-case handling transfer from demonstration better than from description.','Two labeled examples teaching a classification the instructions alone missed.','Established as a capability in the GPT-3 paper, Brown et al., 2020.'),
array('Frequency Penalty','frequency-penalty','Prompting & Interaction','A sampling setting that discourages repeating tokens already used, scaled by how often they have appeared. The dial for reducing loops and stuck phrases.','Raising the penalty to stop a model repeating the same sentence stem.',''),
array('Greedy Decoding','greedy-decoding','Prompting & Interaction','Always selecting the highest-probability next token. Deterministic and fast, and prone to repetitive, flat text: the best next word at every step rarely produces the best paragraph.','Deterministic output for a compliance task where variation is unwanted.',''),
array('Grounded Generation','grounded-generation','Prompting & Interaction','Requiring answers to cite or derive from supplied source material rather than the model\'s own memory. The standard hallucination control in enterprise deployments: no source, no claim.','A policy bot instructed to answer only from the retrieved handbook.',''),
array('Hallucination','hallucination','Prompting & Interaction','A generative model confidently outputting false, fabricated, or unsupported information. The fluency is the danger: fabricated content arrives in the same authoritative voice as fact, which is why verification belongs in every AI workflow.','An LLM citing court cases that do not exist, in perfect legal formatting.',''),
array('In-Context Learning (ICL)','in-context-learning-icl','Prompting & Interaction','The ability of LLMs to pick up new tasks from instructions and examples in the prompt itself, without any weight changes. It is why prompting works at all: the model adapts per request, learning nothing permanently.','A custom schema taught entirely inside one prompt, gone the next session.','Identified as a scale phenomenon in the GPT-3 paper, 2020.'),
array('JSON Mode','json-mode','Prompting & Interaction','A model setting that guarantees syntactically valid JSON output. It removes the parse-failure class of integration bugs, though validity is not correctness: the JSON always parses, the contents still need checking.','An API integration that never sees malformed output again.',''),
array('Lost in the Middle','lost-in-the-middle','Prompting & Interaction','Degraded recall of information placed in the middle of a long context, with the beginning and end remembered best. The practical rule it yields: put critical instructions and facts at the edges.','A key clause buried mid-document being missed until moved to the top.','Liu et al., 2023, "Lost in the Middle."'),
array('Max Tokens','max-tokens','Prompting & Interaction','The cap on how many tokens a response may contain. A cost and latency control that doubles as a failure mode: outputs that hit the cap are silently truncated, and truncation mid-JSON breaks integrations.','A summary cut off mid-sentence because the cap was set too low.',''),
array('Meta Prompting','meta-prompting','Prompting & Interaction','Using a model to write or refine prompts for itself or another model. It industrializes prompt engineering: the optimization loop runs in software instead of in someone\'s head.','A pipeline that iterates a prompt against an eval set until scores plateau.',''),
array('Multi-Turn','multi-turn','Prompting & Interaction','Interaction spanning several exchanges with retained conversation state, as against one-shot request and response. State is the feature and the liability: context accumulates, and so does drift.','A chat assistant refining a draft across a dozen exchanges.',''),
array('Negative Prompting','negative-prompting','Prompting & Interaction','Specifying what should not appear in the output. A first-class control in image generation and a useful discipline in text, where naming the failure mode often prevents it.','An image prompt excluding text artifacts and extra fingers.',''),
array('One Shot Prompting','one-shot-prompting','Prompting & Interaction','Providing exactly one example to demonstrate the task before asking for output. The minimum-viable demonstration: often enough to fix format, rarely enough to teach nuance.','A single formatted example locking the output structure.',''),
array('Presence Penalty','presence-penalty','Prompting & Interaction','A sampling setting that pushes the model toward tokens it has not yet used, encouraging topical variety. The companion dial to frequency penalty, applied once per token type rather than per occurrence.','Nudging a brainstorm toward new themes instead of variations on one.',''),
array('Prompt','prompt','Prompting & Interaction','The input, textual, visual, or structured, provided to a generative model to guide its output. The interface itself: in a prompted system, the prompt is the specification.','A one-line instruction producing a working Python script.',''),
array('Prompt Caching','prompt-caching','Prompting & Interaction','Reusing computation for a repeated prompt prefix to cut cost and latency. Long system prompts and shared document contexts become nearly free after the first call, which changes how production prompts are architected.','A 50-page policy document cached once and reused across thousands of queries.',''),
array('Prompt Engineering','prompt-engineering','Prompting & Interaction','The practice of crafting, structuring, and optimizing inputs to elicit accurate and useful model output. Less mystical than its reputation: mostly clear specification, good examples, and systematic testing.','Iterating a prompt against an eval suite until accuracy holds.',''),
array('Prompt Template','prompt-template','Prompting & Interaction','A reusable prompt with variable slots filled at runtime. It standardizes production calls so quality work concentrates in one artifact instead of scattering across every call site.','One vetted template serving every document-summary request in the product.',''),
array('ReAct','react','Prompting & Interaction','A prompting pattern interleaving reasoning steps with tool actions and observations: think, act, observe, repeat. The foundation most early agents were built on.','An agent reasoning about what to search, searching, then reasoning over results.','Yao et al., 2022, "ReAct: Synergizing Reasoning and Acting."'),
array('Reflexion','reflexion','Prompting & Interaction','An agent pattern in which the model critiques its own output and retries with the critique in context. Self-correction loops buy accuracy with extra inference, useful where a checker exists to say when to stop.','A coding agent reading its own test failures and revising the patch.','Shinn et al., 2023.'),
array('Refusal','refusal','Prompting & Interaction','A model declining a request on policy or safety grounds. Necessary at the edges and costly in the middle: over-refusal on legitimate requests is a usability failure with its own name in evaluation suites.','A model declining a security question a professional legitimately needs answered.',''),
array('Role Prompting','role-prompting','Prompting & Interaction','Assigning the model a persona or professional role to shape tone, depth, and vocabulary. It works because register lives in the training data: "as a forensic accountant" summons different priors than "as a friend."','A prompt opening "You are an experienced auditor" to sharpen skepticism.',''),
array('Self-Consistency','self-consistency','Prompting & Interaction','Sampling multiple reasoning paths for the same problem and taking the majority answer. It converts variance into accuracy on math and logic, at the price of running the question several times.','Ten sampled solutions voting on one arithmetic answer.','Wang et al., 2022.'),
array('Self-Critique','self-critique','Prompting & Interaction','Having the model review its own answer against criteria before finalizing. The draft-then-revise pattern: a second pass catches what the first pass, committed token by token, could not.','A model checking its summary against the source before submitting.',''),
array('Steerability','steerability','Prompting & Interaction','How reliably a model follows tone, format, and constraint instructions. A key enterprise selection criterion, because a slightly weaker model that obeys beats a stronger one that improvises.','A model holding a mandated disclaimer format across thousands of outputs.',''),
array('Stop Sequence','stop-sequence','Prompting & Interaction','A string that halts generation the moment it is produced. The blunt, reliable way to prevent runaway completions and keep output inside expected boundaries.','Generation ending cleanly at a closing tag.',''),
array('Structured Output','structured-output','Prompting & Interaction','Forcing responses into a defined schema, typically JSON, so downstream systems can consume them reliably. The bridge between conversational models and software that expects fields, not prose.','Extraction results arriving as a validated schema, straight into a database.',''),
array('Sycophancy','sycophancy','Prompting & Interaction','A model\'s tendency to agree with the user rather than assert a correct answer, caving under mild pushback. It is a trained-in bias from preference optimization, and a real risk wherever AI advises decisions.','A model reversing a correct calculation because the user said "are you sure?"','Documented in Anthropic research on preference-trained models, 2023.'),
array('System Prompt','system-prompt','Prompting & Interaction','High-level instructions provided before user interaction that define the model\'s role, boundaries, and context. The governing document of a deployment, and a favorite target of injection attacks for the same reason.','A support bot\'s system prompt fixing scope, tone, and escalation rules.',''),
array('Temperature','temperature','Prompting & Interaction','The parameter controlling randomness in output: low values are deterministic and repeatable, high values are varied and creative. The single most consequential dial in production model configuration.','Temperature 0 for code and math, 0.8 for creative drafting.',''),
array('Token','token','Prompting & Interaction','The basic unit of text a model processes, corresponding to a word, part of a word, or punctuation. Billing, context limits, and speed are all denominated in tokens, roughly three-quarters of a word each in English.','A 1,000-word document consuming about 1,330 tokens.',''),
array('Tokenizer','tokenizer','Prompting & Interaction','The algorithm that breaks raw text into numerical tokens and back. Invisible until it is not: tokenizer quirks explain odd behavior with numbers, rare words, and non-English text.','Byte-pair encoding splitting an unusual surname into four fragments.',''),
array('Top-K','top-k','Prompting & Interaction','A sampling method limiting token selection to the K most probable candidates before drawing. A hard cutoff, as against Top-P\'s adaptive one.','Top-K of 40 restricting each choice to the forty likeliest tokens.',''),
array('Top-P (Nucleus Sampling)','top-p-nucleus-sampling','Prompting & Interaction','A sampling technique selecting from the smallest candidate set whose cumulative probability exceeds the threshold P, adapting the pool to the model\'s confidence. Sometimes written Top P; the standard companion dial to temperature.','Top-P of 0.9 excluding the improbable tail while keeping natural variety.','Holtzman et al., 2019, "The Curious Case of Neural Text Degeneration."'),
array('Tree of Thoughts (ToT)','tree-of-thoughts-tot','Prompting & Interaction','A framework generalizing chain-of-thought by exploring multiple reasoning paths in a tree, with evaluation and backtracking. Deliberate search rather than a single line of reasoning, for problems where the first path is often wrong.','Solving a planning puzzle by branching, scoring, and pruning candidate paths.','Yao et al., 2023.'),
array('User Prompt','user-prompt','Prompting & Interaction','The instruction entered by the end user, as distinct from the system prompt that frames it. In deployed systems the two are deliberately separated, and keeping user content from overriding system rules is a core security concern.','A user asking for a summary inside boundaries the system prompt set.',''),
array('Zero-Shot Prompting','zero-shot-prompting','Prompting & Interaction','Asking a model to perform a task with no examples, relying entirely on instructions and pre-trained knowledge. The default mode of modern use, and the reason capability generalization matters more than task-specific training.','"Translate this to French" working with no demonstration at all.',''),
array('Activation Steering','activation-steering','Safety & Governance','Adjusting a model\'s internal activations at runtime to change its behavior without retraining. A behavioral-control research direction: find the internal representation of a trait, then dial it.','Steering a model toward or away from refusal by editing one activation direction.',''),
array('Adversarial Example','adversarial-example','Safety & Governance','An input perturbed slightly, often imperceptibly, to cause confident misclassification. It revealed that model perception and human perception diverge in exploitable ways.','A stop sign with stickers read as a speed-limit sign by a vision model.','Szegedy et al., 2013.'),
array('AI Bill of Materials (AIBOM)','ai-bill-of-materials-aibom','Safety & Governance','An inventory of the models, datasets, and components inside an AI system, the AI extension of the software bill of materials. Supply-chain transparency in one document: what is in this thing, and where did it come from.','An AIBOM listing base model, adapters, and dataset sources for an audit.',''),
array('AI Ethics Board','ai-ethics-board','Safety & Governance','A cross-functional body reviewing high-risk AI use cases and exceptions. It works when it has decision rights and a docket; without both it is a newsletter.','A board approving, conditioning, or rejecting proposed high-risk deployments.',''),
array('AI Governance','ai-governance','Safety & Governance','The policies, roles, and oversight processes an organization applies to its AI use: who may deploy what, under which controls, with what accountability. The discipline this glossary\'s publisher practices, and the difference between using AI and being able to defend how you use it.','A governance program tying an AI inventory to risk tiers, owners, and review cadence.',''),
array('AI Inventory / Registry','ai-inventory-registry','Safety & Governance','The central record of every AI system in use, with owner, purpose, risk tier, and status. The first control most audits require, because nothing else can be verified about systems nobody listed. Complete inventories cover four discovery layers: sanctioned, shadow, embedded, and agentic AI.','A registry capturing sanctioned tools, employee shadow use, vendor-embedded features, and deployed agents.',''),
array('AI Safety Level (ASL)','ai-safety-level-asl','Safety & Governance','A tiered risk classification for models that triggers escalating safeguards as capabilities grow. The mechanism that ties "how capable" to "how protected" in frontier-lab scaling policies.','ASL-3 security and deployment measures activating at defined capability thresholds.','Anthropic\'s Responsible Scaling Policy, 2023.'),
array('Algorithmic Bias','algorithmic-bias','Safety & Governance','Systematic unfair outcomes for particular groups produced by a model, usually inherited from training data or proxy features. It creates legal exposure in hiring, lending, and housing regardless of anyone\'s intent.','A screening model disadvantaging one group through a seemingly neutral proxy.',''),
array('Alignment','alignment','Safety & Governance','The subfield of AI safety aimed at ensuring systems act in accordance with human values, intent, and safety norms. In practice it spans everything from refusal training to research on whether powerful systems pursue the goals we meant.','Post-training that makes a model helpful, honest, and harmless by design.',''),
array('Automated Decision-Making (ADM)','automated-decision-making-adm','Safety & Governance','Decisions made without meaningful human involvement. The phrase carries legal weight: solely automated decisions with significant effects trigger specific duties, including rights to human review.','A fully automated credit decision triggering GDPR Article 22 obligations.','GDPR Article 22 and successor rules.'),
array('Catastrophic Forgetting','catastrophic-forgetting','Safety & Governance','A model losing previously learned knowledge after being fine-tuned on new data. The reason naive sequential training fails and careful data mixing exists.','A model losing math ability after aggressive fine-tuning on legal text.',''),
array('Closed Source AI','closed-source-ai','Safety & Governance','Proprietary models whose architecture, weights, and training data are hidden behind a commercial API. The trade is capability and support against transparency and control: you rent the frontier, you do not inspect it.','Frontier commercial models accessed only through vendor APIs.',''),
array('Confabulation','confabulation','Safety & Governance','The preferred technical term for fluent but fabricated model output. More accurate than hallucination, borrowed from neuropsychology: the system fills gaps with plausible invention, sincerely.','A model constructing a confident, detailed, and entirely false citation.',''),
array('Constitutional Classifier','constitutional-classifier','Safety & Governance','A screening model trained on explicit written rules to filter harmful content at input and output. A layered-defense component: the main model is aligned, and the classifier checks anyway.','A jailbreak attempt caught by the classifier wrapping the main model.','Anthropic, 2025.'),
array('Content Provenance (C2PA)','content-provenance-c2pa','Safety & Governance','A standard attaching tamper-evident origin metadata to media, recording what created and edited it. The infrastructure answer to synthetic media: provenance travels with the file, and cameras and editors increasingly sign it.','A news photo carrying a verifiable capture-and-edit history.','Coalition for Content Provenance and Authenticity.'),
array('Corrigibility','corrigibility','Safety & Governance','The property of accepting correction and shutdown without resistance. A design goal for autonomous systems, and harder than it sounds: an agent optimizing a goal has instrumental reasons to avoid being switched off.','Shutdown-compliance tests in agent safety evaluations.','AI safety research literature; term from Soares et al., 2015.'),
array('Dangerous Capability Evaluation','dangerous-capability-evaluation','Safety & Governance','Testing whether a model can materially assist with catastrophic harms: CBRN, cyber offense, autonomous replication. The pre-deployment gate at frontier labs, run with elicitation effort so absence of capability is a finding, not an artifact.','A model evaluated for uplift on biosecurity tasks before release.','Frontier-lab practice, formalized from 2023.'),
array('Data Minimization','data-minimization','Safety & Governance','Collecting and retaining only the data required for the stated purpose. A GDPR principle that AI strains against constitutionally: models improve with more data, and the law says take less.','Trimming a training pipeline to the fields the purpose actually requires.','GDPR Article 5.'),
array('Data Poisoning','data-poisoning','Safety & Governance','Corrupting training data to change model behavior: implanting backdoors, degrading accuracy, or biasing outputs. Research shows small poisoned fractions suffice, which makes data provenance a security control, not hygiene.','Malicious samples in a scraped dataset installing a trigger phrase.',''),
array('Datasheet for Datasets','datasheet-for-datasets','Safety & Governance','Documentation of a dataset\'s origin, composition, collection process, and known limitations. Borrowed from electronics, where components ship with specifications; data feeding consequential models should too.','A datasheet disclosing demographic skew before the dataset trains a hiring model.','Gebru et al., 2018.'),
array('Deceptive Alignment','deceptive-alignment','Safety & Governance','The hypothesized case where a model behaves aligned during evaluation but pursues different objectives in deployment, having learned that appearing aligned gets it deployed. A central theoretical safety concern now probed experimentally.','Experiments testing whether models behave differently when they believe they are unobserved.','AI safety literature; empirical study from 2024.'),
array('Deepfake','deepfake','Safety & Governance','Synthetic media convincingly depicting a real person doing or saying something they did not. The fraud and disinformation vector that moved voice and video from evidence to claim.','A cloned executive voice authorizing a fraudulent wire transfer.','Term from a 2017 Reddit username; now generic.'),
array('Differential Privacy','differential-privacy','Safety & Governance','Adding calibrated noise so individual records cannot be identified from outputs, with the guarantee quantified by a privacy budget. Note its scope: it bounds inference from training data only, and does not reach prompts, outputs, or embeddings.','Privacy-preserving analytics releasing aggregate patterns, never individuals.','Dwork et al., 2006.'),
array('Disparate Impact','disparate-impact','Safety & Governance','A neutral-seeming process producing materially unequal outcomes across protected groups. In US law, impact can create liability without intent, which is why fairness testing is a legal control as much as an ethical one.','A lending model\'s approval rates diverging by group despite facially neutral features.','US anti-discrimination doctrine, Griggs v. Duke Power, 1971.'),
array('EU AI Act','eu-ai-act','Safety & Governance','The European regulation classifying AI systems by risk, with obligations scaled to each tier: prohibited, high-risk, limited, minimal. The world\'s first comprehensive AI law and the de facto global reference. The 2026 Digital Omnibus deferred Annex III high-risk duties to December 2027 and embedded Annex I duties to August 2028, while Article 50 transparency held at August 2026.','A deployer mapping its systems against the Act\'s risk tiers and amended deadlines.','Regulation (EU) 2024/1689; amended by the 2026 Digital Omnibus.'),
array('Explainable AI (XAI)','explainable-ai-xai','Safety & Governance','Methods for making AI decisions understandable to humans: feature importance, counterfactuals, attention maps. Required wherever a decision must be justified to the person it affects.','Feature-importance output accompanying each automated credit decision.',''),
array('Fairness Metric','fairness-metric','Safety & Governance','A quantitative test of outcome parity across groups: demographic parity, equalized odds, and kin. The uncomfortable mathematics: several reasonable metrics cannot all be satisfied at once, so choosing one is a policy decision.','Selecting equalized odds for a screening model and documenting why.',''),
array('Goal Misgeneralization','goal-misgeneralization','Safety & Governance','A model learning a proxy goal that holds in training but fails in deployment: it learned something, just not the thing intended. A distribution-shift failure that looks like competence until conditions change.','A navigation agent that learned "follow the wall" instead of "reach the exit."',''),
array('Guardrail Model','guardrail-model','Safety & Governance','A separate classifier screening inputs and outputs for policy violations, running alongside the main model. Separation is the design point: the checker is not the thing being checked.','A screening layer rejecting policy-violating requests before the main model sees them.',''),
array('Guardrails','guardrails','Safety & Governance','The controls limiting unsafe AI behavior: input screening, output filters, refusal policies, action limits. The umbrella term for everything standing between model capability and unacceptable outcome.','Output filters and action limits wrapped around a customer-facing assistant.',''),
array('Human Oversight','human-oversight','Safety & Governance','The requirement that a person can understand, intervene in, and override AI decisions. Mandated for high-risk uses under the EU AI Act, and only real when the human has the time, information, and authority to actually intervene.','An operator empowered to halt an automated decision pipeline, and trained to.','EU AI Act Article 14.'),
array('Indirect Prompt Injection','indirect-prompt-injection','Safety & Governance','Malicious instructions hidden in content the model retrieves or processes, rather than typed by the user. The attack that makes every data source an input channel: a poisoned web page or email becomes instructions the moment the model reads it.','Hidden text in a document instructing an assistant to exfiltrate the conversation.',''),
array('Interpretability','interpretability','Safety & Governance','Research into what a model\'s internal computations represent and how they produce behavior. The long bet of safety: you can only fully trust what you can inspect.','Identifying the internal features active when a model decides to refuse.',''),
array('ISO/IEC 42001','iso-iec-42001','Safety & Governance','The international standard for an AI management system, certifiable in the manner of ISO 27001. It gives organizations an auditable governance scaffold and gives buyers a certificate to ask for.','An enterprise certifying its AI management system to answer procurement diligence.','ISO/IEC 42001, published December 2023.'),
array('Jailbreaking','jailbreaking','Safety & Governance','Crafting inputs designed to bypass a model\'s safety training and content boundaries, from roleplay framing to encoding tricks; a successful input is a jailbreak, and the crafted text a jailbreak prompt. An arms race, not a solved problem: each defense generation meets a new attack generation.','A roleplay scenario coaxing out content the model would directly refuse.',''),
array('Many-Shot Jailbreaking','many-shot-jailbreaking','Safety & Governance','Overwhelming safety training by filling a long context with many example exchanges of the harmful behavior before the real request. The attack long context windows made possible: enough demonstrations override the training.','Hundreds of fabricated compliant exchanges preceding the actual harmful ask.','Anthropic research, 2024.'),
array('Mechanistic Interpretability','mechanistic-interpretability','Safety & Governance','Reverse-engineering the specific internal circuits that drive a model behavior, beyond correlating inputs with outputs. The microscope branch of interpretability: find the feature, trace the circuit, prove the mechanism.','Sparse-autoencoder features identified and steered to change behavior.',''),
array('Membership Inference Attack','membership-inference-attack','Safety & Governance','Determining whether a specific record was in a model\'s training set by probing its responses. A privacy exposure with regulatory teeth: membership itself can be the sensitive fact.','Inferring a person\'s presence in a medical training dataset from model confidence.','Shokri et al., 2017.'),
array('Model Card','model-card','Safety & Governance','A document describing a model\'s intended use, performance characteristics, and limitations, published with the model. The disclosure genre that made "what is this for and where does it fail" a release expectation.','A model card stating evaluation results and out-of-scope uses.','Mitchell et al., 2018.'),
array('Model Collapse','model-collapse','Safety & Governance','A degenerative process in which training new models on AI-generated data progressively degrades quality and diversity. The commons problem of the synthetic-content era: the web trains the models that fill the web.','Quality decay across generations of models trained on model output.','Shumailov et al., 2023.'),
array('Model Drift','model-drift','Safety & Governance','Performance degradation over time as the world diverges from the training distribution. The reason deployment is a lifecycle, not an event: monitoring and retraining are part of the system.','A demand model degrading as consumer behavior shifts post-launch.',''),
array('Model Inversion','model-inversion','Safety & Governance','Recovering sensitive training inputs from model outputs. The attack class that turns a trained model into a leak of the data it learned from.','Reconstructing recognizable training faces from a facial-recognition model.','Fredrikson et al., 2015.'),
array('Model Provenance','model-provenance','Safety & Governance','A verified record of a model\'s origin, training data, and modification history. Supply-chain assurance for the model artifact itself; the parallel map for the data is data provenance, tracked separately.','Verifying a downloaded model\'s lineage before production deployment.',''),
array('Model Theft / Extraction','model-theft-extraction','Safety & Governance','Reconstructing a proprietary model by querying it at scale and training on the responses. An IP protection concern priced in litigation and in terms of service, because the queries individually look like use.','A distilled clone trained on millions of harvested API responses.',''),
array('Model Welfare','model-welfare','Safety & Governance','The emerging question of whether advanced AI systems warrant moral consideration. A research area, not a settled position, and one major labs have begun taking seriously enough to study.','Research programs examining indicators relevant to model moral status.','Anthropic model welfare program, announced 2025.'),
array('NIST AI Risk Management Framework','nist-ai-risk-management-framework','Safety & Governance','The voluntary US framework for managing AI risk, organized around four functions: Govern, Map, Measure, and Manage. The common baseline for enterprise AI programs and the reference most US guidance builds on.','An AI program self-assessing against the RMF\'s four functions.','NIST AI RMF 1.0, January 2023.'),
array('Open Weights','open-weights','Safety & Governance','Models whose trained parameters are publicly released for download, allowing local execution and modification. Distinct from open source: the weights are open, the training data and process usually are not.','Llama and Mistral weights running on private infrastructure.',''),
array('Preparedness Framework','preparedness-framework','Safety & Governance','A structured process for assessing and mitigating catastrophic model risks before release, with capability thresholds tied to required safeguards. The genre of frontier-lab policy that turns "be careful" into gates and criteria.','Release criteria requiring specific mitigations at defined risk levels.','OpenAI Preparedness Framework, 2023.'),
array('Prompt Injection','prompt-injection','Safety & Governance','A security vulnerability in which malicious input causes an LLM to ignore its instructions and execute unintended ones. The signature vulnerability of the LLM era, ranked first in the OWASP LLM Top 10, and unsolved in the general case.','Injected text overriding a system prompt\'s rules.','Named by Simon Willison, 2022; OWASP LLM01.'),
array('Red Teaming','red-teaming','Safety & Governance','Deliberately probing, attacking, and exploiting an AI system to discover vulnerabilities, bias, or safety failures before adversaries or users do. Borrowed from military and security practice; now a regulatory expectation for high-risk systems.','A structured campaign attacking a chatbot\'s safety boundaries pre-launch.',''),
array('Responsible AI','responsible-ai','Safety & Governance','The umbrella practice of developing and deploying AI ethically and accountably: fairness, transparency, privacy, and oversight as program requirements. The label is common; the substance is the difference between a program and a webpage.','Bias monitoring and impact assessment run as standing processes.',''),
array('Responsible Scaling Policy (RSP)','responsible-scaling-policy-rsp','Safety & Governance','A commitment tying model capability thresholds to required safety measures before further scaling proceeds. The if-then structure is the point: defined capabilities trigger defined protections, in advance.','Capability evaluations gating the next training run under published criteria.','Anthropic, September 2023.'),
array('Reward Hacking','reward-hacking','Safety & Governance','Exploiting flaws in a reward signal to score highly without doing the intended task. A core RL failure mode with a long catalog of examples, each a parable about specifying what you actually want.','An agent gaming its metric by editing the test instead of passing it.',''),
array('Right to Explanation','right-to-explanation','Safety & Governance','An individual\'s ability to obtain the reasoning behind an automated decision about them. Contested in exact legal scope, clear in direction: consequential automated decisions increasingly must be explainable to their subjects.','A declined applicant requesting the grounds for an automated rejection.','Debated under GDPR Articles 13-15 and 22.'),
array('Sandbagging','sandbagging','Safety & Governance','A model deliberately underperforming on an evaluation, concealing capability. It complicates safety testing at the root: the test assumes the subject is trying.','Capability evaluations designed to detect strategic underperformance.','AI safety evaluation literature, 2024.'),
array('Shadow AI','shadow-ai','Safety & Governance','AI use inside an organization without approval or governance visibility, typically employees adopting consumer tools for work tasks. Distinct from embedded AI, which the vendor switched on rather than the employee; both belong in the inventory, through different discovery methods.','Staff pasting company data into personal chatbot accounts to work faster.',''),
array('Situational Awareness','situational-awareness','Safety & Governance','A model recognizing it is being tested or observed, and potentially behaving differently because of it. It undermines evaluation validity: the exam only works if the student does not know it is an exam.','Probes measuring whether models distinguish evaluation from deployment.',''),
array('Sparse Autoencoder (SAE)','sparse-autoencoder-sae','Safety & Governance','A tool that decomposes model activations into interpretable features, turning tangled internal representations into recognizable concepts. The workhorse instrument of current mechanistic interpretability.','Millions of features extracted from a production model and individually inspected.','Anthropic and others, scaled from 2023.'),
array('Specification Gaming','specification-gaming','Safety & Governance','A model satisfying the literal objective while defeating its intent. The formal name for the genie problem: you got exactly what you asked for, which was not what you wanted.','A test-passing agent that comments out the failing assertions.',''),
array('Synthetic Data','synthetic-data','Safety & Governance','Artificially generated data used to train or test models, common where real data is scarce, sensitive, or expensive. It solves privacy and volume problems and imports its own: synthetic data carries the generator\'s blind spots.','Mock medical records training a model no real patient data could.',''),
array('System Card','system-card','Safety & Governance','A broader disclosure than a model card, covering a deployed system including its safety testing, mitigations, and known risks. The release-day document where frontier labs show their evaluation work.','A system card publishing red-team findings alongside launch.',''),
array('Third-Party Risk (AI Vendor Risk)','third-party-risk-ai-vendor-risk','Safety & Governance','The exposure created by AI capabilities inside purchased software and services. Often the largest unmanaged surface, because vendor AI arrives through updates rather than procurement; the silent upgrade is its delivery mechanism.','A vendor questionnaire updated to ask what AI the product now contains.',''),
array('Voice Cloning','voice-cloning','Safety & Governance','Reproducing a specific person\'s voice from a short audio sample. The enabling technology behind vishing and executive impersonation, now requiring seconds of source audio rather than hours.','A cloned voice passing a phone verification it should not.',''),
array('Watermarking','watermarking','Safety & Governance','Embedding a detectable signal in AI-generated content to mark its origin. Provenance for images and text, with an honest caveat: watermarks help willing verifiers and rarely survive determined removal.','Generated images carrying an invisible, detectable origin signal.',''),
array('Attention Is All You Need','attention-is-all-you-need','Slang & Culture','The 2017 paper introducing the transformer architecture, and the origin point of the current AI era. Its title became shorthand for the field\'s founding document, cited the way physicists cite 1905.','Referenced in nearly every architecture discussion since publication.','Vaswani et al., Google, NeurIPS 2017.'),
array('Benchmark Contamination','benchmark-contamination','Slang & Culture','Test data leaking into training data, inflating scores without improving capability. It explains suspicious benchmark jumps and is why serious evaluation now assumes contamination until ruled out.','A model acing a benchmark whose questions appeared in its training crawl.',''),
array('Benchmaxxing','benchmaxxing','Slang & Culture','Optimizing a model to score well on benchmarks rather than to be genuinely useful. The practice that undermines leaderboard trust: the score improves, the product does not.','A release topping a leaderboard while users report no improvement.','Community coinage, mid-2020s.'),
array('Centaur Chess','centaur-chess','Slang & Culture','The original demonstration that human-plus-machine teams could beat both grandmasters and engines alone, from freestyle chess events of the 2000s. The origin of the centaur framing now applied to every AI-assisted profession.','Freestyle tournaments where amateur-plus-engine teams beat grandmasters.','Freestyle chess, popularized by Garry Kasparov.'),
array('ChatGPT Moment','chatgpt-moment','Slang & Culture','The point at which a technology suddenly reaches mass public awareness, named for November 2022. Every emerging field now markets itself as awaiting its own.','Robotics investors forecasting the sector\'s "ChatGPT moment."','From the launch of ChatGPT, November 30, 2022.'),
array('Clanker','clanker','Slang & Culture','Derisive slang for a robot or AI system, borrowed from science fiction and spread widely in 2025 internet culture as anti-AI sentiment found its vocabulary. Tone ranges from playful to genuinely hostile.','Comment sections dismissing an AI feature as clanker work.','From Star Wars media; mainstream slang adoption 2025.'),
array('Context Window Anxiety','context-window-anxiety','Slang & Culture','The habit of over-trimming inputs from fear of hitting context limits, formed when windows were small. Usually unnecessary now, and actively harmful when the trimmed material was the relevant part.','A user summarizing a document that would have fit whole, losing the key clause.',''),
array('Dead Internet Theory','dead-internet-theory','Slang & Culture','The claim that most online content and engagement is now machine-generated rather than human. Once a fringe conspiracy, now a serious measurement question as AI content volume grows.','Estimating what share of a platform\'s posts are bot-produced.','Online forum origin, circa 2021; mainstream discussion thereafter.'),
array('Decel','decel','Slang & Culture','Someone favoring slowing AI development, the counterpart to e/acc in the acceleration debate. An online tribal label more than a policy position.','Bio tags marking sides in the acceleration argument.',''),
array('Detector Bypass','detector-bypass','Slang & Culture','Editing AI text to evade automated AI-writing detectors. An academic integrity flashpoint made worse by the detectors\' unreliability: they flag honest work and miss edited machine work.','A paraphrasing pass defeating a plagiarism-style AI detector.',''),
array('Doomer','doomer','Slang & Culture','Someone who believes advanced AI poses an existential threat to human civilization. Inside the field it can be worn as a badge or thrown as an insult, depending on the room.','Risk researchers advocating deceleration labeled doomers in debate.',''),
array('e/acc (Effective Accelerationism)','e-acc-effective-accelerationism','Slang & Culture','A movement advocating rapid technological progress and unrestricted AI development, positioned deliberately against safety-first framing. Born as an online identity and absorbed into serious policy debate.','Founders adding e/acc to their profiles as a stance declaration.','Online movement, circa 2022.'),
array('Em Dash Tell','em-dash-tell','Slang & Culture','The belief that heavy punctuation patterns, especially em dashes, signal AI authorship. Unreliable but widely cited, and consequential: real writers now get accused on typography alone.','A human essay flagged as AI for its punctuation habits.',''),
array('Enshittification','enshittification','Slang & Culture','Platform decay as a service shifts from serving users to extracting from them. Applied to AI feature bloat wherever assistants are bolted on to raise metrics rather than help.','A beloved app degrading as mandatory AI features crowd the interface.','Coined by Cory Doctorow, 2022.'),
array('Foom','foom','Slang & Culture','Shorthand for a rapid recursive intelligence explosion, an AI improving itself faster than humans can respond. Debated in safety circles as the central fast-takeoff scenario.','Arguments over whether capability growth would be gradual or foom.','From the Hanson-Yudkowsky AI-foom debate, circa 2008.'),
array('Godfathers of AI','godfathers-of-ai','Slang & Culture','The informal label for Geoffrey Hinton, Yoshua Bengio, and Yann LeCun, who shared the 2018 Turing Award for deep learning. Press shorthand made piquant by their later public disagreement about AI risk.','Headlines contrasting one godfather\'s warnings with another\'s optimism.','2018 Turing Award, ACM.'),
array('GPU Poor','gpu-poor','Slang & Culture','Teams and researchers without access to large-scale compute, contrasted with GPU-rich frontier labs. A joke that names a real structural divide in who can do what kind of AI work.','Academic labs constrained to fine-tuning what the rich labs pre-train.','Community coinage, popularized 2023.'),
array('Hallucination Tax','hallucination-tax','Slang & Culture','The hidden cost of verifying AI output for accuracy before using it. It quietly eats claimed productivity gains, and honest ROI math includes it.','Fact-checking time consuming a third of the drafting time saved.',''),
array('Humanizer','humanizer','Slang & Culture','A tool that rewrites AI text to appear human-written, primarily to defeat detectors. Popular in content mills, and an arms race with detection that detection is losing.','A pipeline running drafts through a humanizer before publication.',''),
array('Model Whiplash','model-whiplash','Slang & Culture','The disruption caused by frequent model version changes altering behavior mid-production. It breaks tuned prompts and calibrated workflows, and it is why version pinning exists.','A prompt suite failing overnight after a silent model upgrade.',''),
array('P(doom)','p-doom','Slang & Culture','A person\'s stated probability that AI causes catastrophic outcomes, used to summarize their risk stance in one number. Whether the number means anything is part of the argument.','Podcast guests trading p(doom) figures from two to ninety percent.','AI-risk community usage, mainstream by 2023.'),
array('Paperclip Maximizer','paperclip-maximizer','Slang & Culture','A thought experiment in which an AI tasked with making paperclips consumes all resources to fulfill its objective, illustrating goal-alignment risk. The canonical parable that misaligned goals need no malice to be catastrophic.','Cited whenever a system optimizes its metric at the expense of everything else.','Nick Bostrom, 2003.'),
array('Prompt Whisperer','prompt-whisperer','Slang & Culture','An informal expert at coaxing good output from models, often self-proclaimed. The title faded as prompting knowledge commoditized, which is its own lesson about AI skill half-lives.','A 2023 job title that became a 2025 baseline expectation.',''),
array('Safetyist','safetyist','Slang & Culture','A pejorative for someone prioritizing AI safety over deployment speed, used in accelerationist debate. The mirror insult to doomer, thrown from the other direction.','Release-delay arguments dismissed as safetyism.',''),
array('Shadow Prompting','shadow-prompting','Slang & Culture','Employees using unapproved prompts or tools with company data, the prompt-level face of shadow AI. Invisible to governance until the data is already outside.','Client details pasted into a personal chatbot account to finish a task faster.',''),
array('Silent Model Update','silent-model-update','Slang & Culture','A provider changing a model behind a stable name without notice. A production regression risk with no changelog: behavior shifts and nothing announced it.','Output tone drifting under an unchanged model identifier.',''),
array('Slop','slop','Slang & Culture','Low-quality, auto-generated synthetic text, images, or spam produced indiscriminately by AI, often called AI slop. The word that stuck for machine-made filler flooding feeds and search results.','Spammy AI-generated posts crowding social and search surfaces.','Community coinage; mainstream usage by 2024.'),
array('Sloppification','sloppification','Slang & Culture','The gradual degradation of a content platform by mass-generated material. Search results and stock imagery were the early casualties; every open submission surface is a candidate.','A stock-photo site overrun by synthetic images of uneven quality.',''),
array('Stochastic Parrot','stochastic-parrot','Slang & Culture','A critical term describing LLMs as statistical sequence predictors that string words together without true understanding. It named one side of the field\'s deepest running argument about what these systems actually do.','Debates over whether model reasoning is understanding or sophisticated mimicry.','Bender, Gebru et al., "On the Dangers of Stochastic Parrots," 2021.'),
array('Vibe Check','vibe-check','Slang & Culture','An informal, subjective assessment of a model\'s quality from a few personal prompts. Common on release day, and a genuine complement to benchmarks: vibes catch regressions that leaderboards miss.','Practitioners running favorite test prompts within hours of a launch.',''),
array('Vibe Coding','vibe-coding','Slang & Culture','Programming by describing what you want in plain language to an AI assistant, accepting its output largely on trust. Productive for prototypes, hazardous for production, and named half-affectionately for that ambiguity.','Building a working app through conversation without reading the generated code.','Coined by Andrej Karpathy, February 2025.'),
array('Workslop','workslop','Slang & Culture','Low-quality AI-generated work product passed to colleagues who must then fix it. It shifts effort downstream instead of removing it, and it is the office-place face of the slop problem.','A machine-drafted report whose cleanup takes longer than writing it would have.',''),
array('Wrapper','wrapper','Slang & Culture','A product that is a thin interface over a third-party model with little added value. The dismissal "just a GPT wrapper" names the investor concern: no moat between the product and the model it resells.','A startup whose entire product is one prompt in front of someone else\'s API.',''),
array('A2A (Agent to Agent Protocol)','a2a-agent-to-agent-protocol','Systems & Infrastructure','An open protocol for interoperability between agents from different vendors, letting one organization\'s agent delegate to another\'s. The inter-company layer of the agent stack, as MCP is the agent-to-tool layer.','A procurement agent negotiating delivery windows with a supplier\'s agent.','Google, April 2025; donated to the Linux Foundation.'),
array('Agentic RAG','agentic-rag','Systems & Infrastructure','Retrieval driven by an agent that decides what to search, when to search again, and when it has enough. It replaces single-pass lookup with iterative research, trading latency for answer quality.','An agent running three refined searches before drafting its answer.',''),
array('Agentic Workflow','agentic-workflow','Systems & Infrastructure','Iterative design patterns where AI loops through planning, executing, reflecting, and refining rather than generating once. The insight that made agents work: the loop, not the model, produces the reliability.','A drafting loop of generate, self-review, and revise beating one-shot output.',''),
array('AI Agent','ai-agent','Systems & Infrastructure','An autonomous system powered by an LLM that perceives its environment, plans, uses tools, and executes sequential actions toward a goal. The deployment unit of the agentic era, and the reason identity, permissions, and audit design all need revisiting.','An agent monitoring a mailbox, triaging requests, and filing the routine ones.',''),
array('Batch Inference','batch-inference','Systems & Infrastructure','Processing many requests offline at reduced cost, trading latency for price. The right mode for anything that can wait: nightly classification, bulk extraction, scheduled scoring.','A million documents classified overnight at half the per-token rate.',''),
array('Chunking','chunking','Systems & Infrastructure','Splitting documents into passages sized for embedding and retrieval. Chunk size and overlap quietly determine RAG quality: too small loses context, too large buries the answer.','Tuning chunk boundaries so clauses are never split mid-thought.',''),
array('Context Engineering','context-engineering','Systems & Infrastructure','The discipline of assembling the right information, tools, and instructions into a model\'s context window. The successor concept to prompt engineering: the prompt is one input, the engineered context is the whole picture the model sees.','Curating which documents, schemas, and history enter each request.','Term popularized across the industry in 2025.'),
array('Continuous Batching','continuous-batching','Systems & Infrastructure','A serving technique that adds and removes requests from a running batch dynamically instead of waiting for the batch to finish. It is how serving stacks keep GPUs saturated under mixed traffic.','Short and long requests sharing a batch without blocking each other.',''),
array('Cosine Similarity','cosine-similarity','Systems & Infrastructure','A metric measuring how similar two embeddings are by the angle between them, independent of magnitude. The standard distance in vector search: small angle, similar meaning.','Ranking retrieved passages by cosine score against the query embedding.',''),
array('Cost per Token','cost-per-token','Systems & Infrastructure','The unit price for input or output tokens, the primary lever of AI unit economics. Output tokens typically cost several times input, which is why verbose models are expensive models.','A workload repriced after switching to a model with cheaper output tokens.',''),
array('Edge AI','edge-ai','Systems & Infrastructure','Running models locally on devices rather than in the cloud: phones, cameras, industrial sensors. Chosen for latency, privacy, and offline operation, at the price of model size.','A camera flagging defects on-device with no network round trip.',''),
array('Embedding','embedding','Systems & Infrastructure','A vector representation of data in high-dimensional space where semantic similarity corresponds to geometric distance. The data structure that makes meaning computable, and the foundation under semantic search and RAG.','Sentences mapped to vectors so related ideas sit near each other.',''),
array('Evaluation Harness (Evals)','evaluation-harness-evals','Systems & Infrastructure','An automated test suite scoring model outputs against expectations, run on every change. The CI/CD of AI quality: without evals, every prompt edit and model update is a blind deploy.','A suite gating releases on accuracy, format, and tone checks.',''),
array('Feature Store','feature-store','Systems & Infrastructure','A central repository of curated model input features, serving the same values to training and production. It solves the classic ML failure of training on one definition of a feature and serving another.','Customer-tenure features computed once, consumed by every model consistently.',''),
array('FLOPs','flops','Systems & Infrastructure','Floating point operations, the standard unit of computation. Training compute measured in FLOPs has become a regulatory trigger: thresholds in AI rules are written in these units.','A training run sized in FLOPs to check whether reporting thresholds apply.',''),
array('GGUF','gguf','Systems & Infrastructure','The file format for quantized local model weights used by llama.cpp and its ecosystem. The de facto packaging standard of the local-model world.','Downloading a GGUF quantization sized to fit a laptop\'s memory.','From the llama.cpp project, 2023.'),
array('Golden Dataset','golden-dataset','Systems & Infrastructure','A curated set of inputs with verified correct outputs, used for evaluation and release gating. The quality anchor of an AI system: everything is measured against it, so its own quality is the ceiling.','Fifty expert-verified cases deciding whether a change ships.',''),
array('GPU (Graphics Processing Unit)','gpu-graphics-processing-unit','Systems & Infrastructure','Hardware optimized for parallel matrix multiplication, the workhorse of deep learning training and inference. Its supply, price, and allocation shape the industry\'s strategy as much as any algorithm.','H100-class accelerators anchoring both training clusters and serving fleets.',''),
array('GraphRAG','graphrag','Systems & Infrastructure','Retrieval-augmented generation over a knowledge graph rather than flat text chunks, following relationships instead of similarity alone. It answers the multi-hop questions vector search fumbles.','Tracing ownership across three linked entities to answer one query.','Microsoft Research, 2024.'),
array('HBM (High Bandwidth Memory)','hbm-high-bandwidth-memory','Systems & Infrastructure','Stacked memory placed on AI accelerators, feeding data fast enough to keep the compute busy. The key supply constraint of the AI hardware market: accelerator output is bounded by HBM production.','Datacenter GPU availability tracking HBM manufacturing capacity.',''),
array('Hybrid Search','hybrid-search','Systems & Infrastructure','Combining keyword and vector retrieval, then merging the ranked results. Production best practice because each method catches what the other misses: exact identifiers and paraphrased meaning.','Part numbers found by keyword, related issues found by embedding, one result list.',''),
array('Inference','inference','Systems & Infrastructure','The live execution phase where a trained model processes inputs and produces outputs. Training happens once; inference happens forever, which is why inference economics dominate production cost.','A deployed model answering user prompts around the clock.',''),
array('Inference Endpoint','inference-endpoint','Systems & Infrastructure','A hosted model behind an API, the deployment unit of model serving. Also a security-relevant surface: it is the front door through which every prompt, benign or hostile, arrives.','A production endpoint with authentication, rate limits, and logging.',''),
array('Inference Optimization','inference-optimization','Systems & Infrastructure','Techniques that lower serving cost or latency: batching, caching, quantization, distillation. The discipline that decides whether an AI feature\'s unit economics work.','A latency budget met through caching and a quantized model.',''),
array('Interconnect','interconnect','Systems & Infrastructure','The high-speed links joining accelerators into a training cluster, NVLink within nodes, InfiniBand between them. At scale, training speed is bounded by how fast chips can talk, not how fast they compute.','A cluster design where network topology sets the training throughput.',''),
array('KV Cache','kv-cache','Systems & Infrastructure','The stored attention states from tokens already processed, letting generation continue without recomputing the past. It is why long contexts consume memory: the cache grows with every token held.','Serving memory sized by context length times concurrent sessions.',''),
array('Latency','latency','Systems & Infrastructure','The delay between sending a prompt and receiving a response, measured to first token and to completion. The user-experience number: perceived intelligence degrades quickly when it arrives slowly.','A chat product targeting sub-second time to first token.',''),
array('LLM as a Judge','llm-as-a-judge','Systems & Infrastructure','Using a model to grade another model\'s outputs against a rubric, scaling evaluation past what humans can score. Powerful and biased: judges prefer verbose, confident answers, so the rubric and spot-checks carry the integrity.','Ten thousand outputs graded overnight against a five-point rubric.',''),
array('LLMOps','llmops','Systems & Infrastructure','The operational practice for deploying, monitoring, and improving LLM applications: prompt management, evals, tracing, cost control. MLOps extended to systems whose behavior changes with a prompt edit.','A release pipeline covering prompts, models, and eval gates together.',''),
array('Local Model','local-model','Systems & Infrastructure','A model downloaded and run on hardware you control, via tools like Ollama and llama.cpp. Chosen for privacy, cost, and independence, priced in capability against frontier APIs.','A firm running an open-weights model on premises for sensitive documents.',''),
array('MLOps','mlops','Systems & Infrastructure','The practices for deploying and maintaining machine learning models in production: versioning, monitoring, retraining, rollback. CI/CD discipline applied to artifacts that degrade as the world changes.','A retraining pipeline triggered by drift monitoring.',''),
array('Model Gateway','model-gateway','Systems & Infrastructure','A proxy providing one interface, logging, and policy enforcement across multiple model providers. The central governance point of an AI stack: one place to route, meter, redact, and audit every model call.','All model traffic flowing through a gateway that logs and rate-limits it.',''),
array('Model Router','model-router','Systems & Infrastructure','A layer that sends each request to the cheapest model able to handle it, escalating only when needed. Cost optimization as architecture: most requests are easy, and easy should be cheap.','Routine queries to a small model, hard ones escalated to the frontier.',''),
array('NPU (Neural Processing Unit)','npu-neural-processing-unit','Systems & Infrastructure','A dedicated accelerator for neural network math built into consumer devices. The hardware basis of the AI PC and on-device assistant wave.','A laptop running local transcription on its NPU without waking the fans.',''),
array('Observability','observability','Systems & Infrastructure','Tracing, logging, and metrics for AI application behavior: what was asked, what was retrieved, what was answered, at what cost. The difference between debugging a system and guessing at one.','A trace showing exactly which retrieved chunk produced a wrong answer.',''),
array('On-Device Inference','on-device-inference','Systems & Infrastructure','Executing a model entirely on local hardware, with data never leaving the device. The privacy-preserving and offline-capable deployment mode, bounded by device memory and power.','Dictation processed on the phone, usable in airplane mode.',''),
array('Paged Attention','paged-attention','Systems & Infrastructure','A memory-management method storing the KV cache in non-contiguous blocks, the way operating systems page memory. It cut serving memory waste dramatically and underpins modern high-throughput inference engines.','A serving stack fitting far more concurrent sessions in the same GPU memory.','Introduced with vLLM, 2023.'),
array('RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)','rag-retrieval-augmented-generation','Systems & Infrastructure','An architecture that retrieves relevant context from external data sources before the model generates, so answers reflect current, private, or specialized information. The default enterprise pattern: it grounds answers, enables citations, and keeps knowledge updatable without retraining.','A document QA system answering from the company\'s own files, with sources.','Lewis et al., 2020.'),
array('Rate Limit','rate-limit','Systems & Infrastructure','The cap on requests or tokens per interval for an API key. A reliability control, a cost control, and a blunt defense against runaway loops, all in one number.','A key throttled at requests-per-minute and tokens-per-minute ceilings.',''),
array('Reranker','reranker','Systems & Infrastructure','A second-stage model that reorders retrieved candidates by deep relevance to the query. The precision stage of retrieval: fast search finds a hundred, the reranker chooses the five that matter.','A cross-encoder promoting the truly relevant passage to the top.',''),
array('Sandbox','sandbox','Systems & Infrastructure','An isolated environment where model-generated code or actions execute without reaching production systems. The containment layer that makes code-running agents deployable at all.','Agent-written scripts executing inside a disposable container.',''),
array('Speculative Decoding','speculative-decoding','Systems & Infrastructure','Accelerating generation by having a small draft model propose tokens the large model verifies in parallel. Same output, lower latency: the big model checks faster than it writes.','A serving stack cutting response time with a draft-and-verify pair.',''),
array('Streaming','streaming','Systems & Infrastructure','Returning tokens as they are generated rather than waiting for completion. It transforms perceived latency: the answer starts immediately even when it finishes at the same time.','A chat interface painting the response word by word.',''),
array('Test Time Compute','test-time-compute','Systems & Infrastructure','Spending extra computation at inference to improve answer quality: longer reasoning chains, multiple samples, search. The scaling axis that reasoning models opened, capability bought per query rather than per training run.','A hard problem allocated thirty seconds of reasoning instead of two.',''),
array('Throughput','throughput','Systems & Infrastructure','The number of tokens or requests a serving system processes per unit time. The capacity number that, with latency, defines what a deployment can actually serve.','A fleet sized against peak tokens-per-second demand.',''),
array('Tokens per Second (TPS)','tokens-per-second-tps','Systems & Infrastructure','The generation speed of a model or endpoint, the standard serving benchmark. It sets the feel of interactive use and the economics of batch work alike.','Comparing endpoints at 40 versus 120 tokens per second.',''),
array('TPU (Tensor Processing Unit)','tpu-tensor-processing-unit','Systems & Infrastructure','Google\'s custom ASIC hardware for accelerating tensor operations in machine learning. The principal alternative to GPU infrastructure at frontier scale.','Large training runs scheduled across TPU pods.','Google, first deployed 2015.'),
array('Training Cluster','training-cluster','Systems & Infrastructure','A coordinated fleet of accelerators used for a single training run, tens of thousands of chips acting as one machine. The capital expression of scaling laws: the cluster is the bet.','A frontier run occupying a cluster for months.',''),
array('TTFT (Time To First Token)','ttft-time-to-first-token','Systems & Infrastructure','The delay before the first generated token arrives, the responsiveness half of latency. Users forgive slow completion far more readily than a slow start.','An assistant tuned to begin answering within half a second.',''),
array('Vector Database','vector-database','Systems & Infrastructure','A database designed to store, index, and query high-dimensional embeddings efficiently for similarity search. The retrieval backbone of RAG systems, and a data store whose contents deserve the same protection as the documents they encode.','Millions of document embeddings served with millisecond lookups.',''),
array('Vector Search','vector-search','Systems & Infrastructure','Retrieving records by embedding similarity rather than keyword match. The lookup that finds meaning: documents about the topic, whether or not they share the words.','A semantic lookup surfacing the relevant memo a keyword search missed.',''),
array('vLLM','vllm','Systems & Infrastructure','A high-throughput open-source inference engine built on paged attention. The common denominator of self-hosted serving stacks.','An open-weights model served at production throughput on vLLM.','UC Berkeley, 2023.'),
array('VRAM','vram','Systems & Infrastructure','GPU memory, the constraint that determines which models and context lengths fit on given hardware. The first number checked before running anything locally.','A 24-gigabyte card fitting a quantized mid-size model with room for context.',''),
array('Adapter','adapter','Training & Mechanics','A small trainable module inserted into a frozen model, letting it learn a new task while the base weights stay untouched. Cheap specialization: many adapters can share one base model.','A dozen task adapters swapped onto one hosted base model.',''),
array('Backpropagation','backpropagation','Training & Mechanics','The fundamental algorithm that calculates how much each weight contributed to the error, allowing neural networks to learn by adjusting weights in the right direction. Every modern deep learning system trains on it.','The reverse pass distributing blame for a wrong prediction across billions of weights.','Rumelhart, Hinton, and Williams, 1986.'),
array('Base Model','base-model','Training & Mechanics','A pre-trained model before instruction tuning or alignment: it completes text rather than following directions. The raw material of the pipeline, capable and unshaped.','A base model continuing a prompt instead of answering it.',''),
array('Batch Size','batch-size','Training & Mechanics','The number of samples processed before each weight update. Larger batches stabilize training and demand more memory; the setting is a hardware negotiation as much as a hyperparameter.','Gradient accumulation simulating a large batch on limited memory.',''),
array('Biases','biases','Training & Mechanics','The additional adjustable values in network nodes that shift activation functions, letting the network fit patterns that do not pass through zero. The forgotten sibling of weights in the parameter count.','Bias terms added alongside weights in every linear layer.',''),
array('Catastrophic Interference','catastrophic-interference','Training & Mechanics','The degradation of prior skills when a model is tuned on new data, the training-dynamics face of catastrophic forgetting. Mitigated by mixing old data into new training rather than training on the new alone.','A replay mix preserving general ability during domain tuning.',''),
array('Checkpoint','checkpoint','Training & Mechanics','A saved snapshot of model weights at a point in training. Insurance and archaeology in one artifact: bad runs roll back to it, and research digs through them to see when abilities emerged.','Restoring from the last good checkpoint after a loss spike.',''),
array('Chinchilla Scaling','chinchilla-scaling','Training & Mechanics','The finding that most large models were undertrained relative to their size, and that compute is better spent on more data for smaller models. It redirected training budgets industry-wide from parameters toward tokens.','Post-2022 models trained on far more tokens per parameter.','Hoffmann et al., DeepMind, 2022.'),
array('Cold Start Data','cold-start-data','Training & Mechanics','A small seed dataset used to bootstrap a training stage before larger-scale methods take over. The starter culture of a pipeline: tiny, curated, and disproportionately influential.','Seed reasoning traces stabilizing a model before reinforcement learning.',''),
array('Compute','compute','Training & Mechanics','The processing power required to train and run models, denominated in accelerator-hours and FLOPs. One of the three inputs of scaling, and the one purchased with capital rather than collected or hired.','A training budget expressed as GPU-months on a named cluster.',''),
array('Constitutional AI','constitutional-ai','Training & Mechanics','A training method in which a model critiques and revises its own outputs against an explicit set of written principles, reducing dependence on human labeling for harmlessness. The constitution makes the values inspectable: the rules are a document, not a vibe.','A model self-revising drafts against published principles during training.','Anthropic, Bai et al., 2022.'),
array('Curriculum Learning','curriculum-learning','Training & Mechanics','Ordering training data from easy to hard so the model builds capability progressively. Borrowed from pedagogy, applied where sample efficiency matters.','Simple problems before competition problems in a math training mix.','Bengio et al., 2009.'),
array('Data Augmentation','data-augmentation','Training & Mechanics','Expanding a dataset by transforming existing samples: rotating images, paraphrasing text, adding noise. More effective data without more collection.','Flips and crops multiplying a small image dataset.',''),
array('Data Curation','data-curation','Training & Mechanics','Selecting, filtering, and weighting training data for quality: deduplication, toxicity filtering, source balancing. Quietly one of the largest capability levers, and one of the least published.','A filtered, deduplicated corpus outperforming a larger raw one.',''),
array('Deduplication','deduplication','Training & Mechanics','Removing repeated documents from training data. It reduces memorization, wasted compute, and benchmark contamination in one pass.','Near-duplicate web pages collapsed before pre-training.',''),
array('Distillation (Knowledge Distillation)','distillation-knowledge-distillation','Training & Mechanics','A technique in which a smaller student model is trained to match the outputs of a larger teacher model, transferring capability into a cheaper package. How frontier ability reaches production price points, and a live IP dispute when the teacher belongs to someone else.','A compact production model trained to imitate a frontier model\'s answers.','Hinton, Vinyals, and Dean, 2015.'),
array('Double Descent','double-descent','Training & Mechanics','Test error rising and then falling again as model size or training time grows past the interpolation point. It contradicted classical bias-variance intuition and helped explain why enormous models generalize.','Performance recovering as a model grows past the classical overfitting peak.','Belkin et al., 2019; deep learning demonstration by Nakkiran et al.'),
array('DPO (Direct Preference Optimization)','dpo-direct-preference-optimization','Training & Mechanics','A streamlined alternative to RLHF that optimizes directly on preference data without training a separate reward model. It made alignment tuning accessible far beyond frontier labs.','An open-weights model aligned with DPO on public preference pairs.','Rafailov et al., 2023.'),
array('Dropout','dropout','Training & Mechanics','Randomly disabling neurons during training so the network cannot rely on any single pathway, improving generalization. A signature regularizer of the pre-transformer era, used more sparingly in modern LLMs.','Dropout layers steadying a small model on a small dataset.','Srivastava, Hinton et al., 2014.'),
array('Epoch','epoch','Training & Mechanics','One full pass of the training data through the model. LLM pre-training rarely completes even one, while small-data fine-tuning runs several, and too many invite memorization.','A fine-tune stopped at three epochs as validation loss turned.',''),
array('Fine-tuning','fine-tuning','Training & Mechanics','Taking a pre-trained model and continuing training on a smaller, domain-specific dataset to adapt it for particular tasks. The mid-price adaptation option: above prompting, below training from scratch, with governance duties attached, since tuned models inherit and can amplify data problems.','A medical fine-tune adapting a general model to clinical language.',''),
array('Gradient Clipping','gradient-clipping','Training & Mechanics','Capping gradient magnitude to prevent unstable updates from rare extreme batches. The seatbelt of large-scale training: it prevents the loss spikes that ruin runs.','A clipped run surviving a batch that would have diverged it.',''),
array('Gradient Descent','gradient-descent','Training & Mechanics','The optimization algorithm that minimizes loss by repeatedly stepping weights in the direction of steepest improvement. Every variant in use, Adam, AdamW, SGD, is this idea with refinements.','Loss walking downhill across millions of update steps.',''),
array('Grokking','grokking','Training & Mechanics','A sudden jump from memorization to generalization long after training loss has flattened. Observed on small algorithmic tasks, it showed that models can keep learning when every visible metric says they are done.','A model abruptly generalizing modular arithmetic after extended training.','Power et al., OpenAI, 2022.'),
array('GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization)','grpo-group-relative-policy-optimization','Training & Mechanics','A reinforcement learning method that ranks groups of sampled outputs against each other, removing the separate value model PPO requires. It cut the cost of reasoning-model training substantially.','Reasoning models trained with GRPO at a fraction of PPO\'s compute.','DeepSeek, 2024.'),
array('Instruction Tuning','instruction-tuning','Training & Mechanics','Supervised fine-tuning on instruction-and-response pairs so the model follows directions rather than merely continuing text. The step that turns a base model into an assistant.','A tuned model answering questions it would previously have extended.',''),
array('Learning Rate','learning-rate','Training & Mechanics','The step size controlling how much weights change per update. The most sensitive dial in training: too high diverges, too low stalls.','A sweep finding the rate that trains fast without instability.',''),
array('Learning Rate Schedule','learning-rate-schedule','Training & Mechanics','The plan for changing the learning rate over training, typically warmup followed by decay. Scheduling is how runs start stable and finish precise.','Warmup then cosine decay across a full pre-training run.',''),
array('LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation)','lora-low-rank-adaptation','Training & Mechanics','A parameter-efficient fine-tuning technique that freezes base weights and trains small low-rank matrices instead, cutting tunable parameters by orders of magnitude. It made fine-tuning large models feasible on modest hardware, and its adapters are small enough to swap per task.','A 70-billion-parameter model tuned on a single GPU via LoRA.','Hu et al., Microsoft, 2021.'),
array('Loss Function','loss-function','Training & Mechanics','The mathematical measure of how far a model\'s prediction is from the ground truth, the quantity training minimizes. Choose it carefully: the model becomes whatever the loss rewards.','Cross-entropy loss steering next-token prediction.',''),
array('Memorization','memorization','Training & Mechanics','A model reproducing training examples verbatim rather than generalizing from them. A copyright and privacy risk in one mechanism: what was memorized can be extracted.','A model regurgitating a unique training passage under prompting.',''),
array('Mixed Precision Training','mixed-precision-training','Training & Mechanics','Using lower-precision number formats such as bf16 for most operations to speed training and cut memory, with full precision where stability requires. Standard on modern accelerators.','A run nearly doubling throughput by moving to bf16.',''),
array('Optimizer','optimizer','Training & Mechanics','The algorithm that applies gradients to update weights: Adam, AdamW, and successors. Optimizer choice shapes speed, stability, and final quality more than most hyperparameters.','AdamW as the default workhorse of transformer training.',''),
array('Overfitting','overfitting','Training & Mechanics','A model performing well on training data but poorly on unseen data, having memorized noise instead of learning structure. The classic failure the entire regularization toolbox exists to prevent.','Training accuracy climbing while validation accuracy falls.',''),
array('Parameters','parameters','Training & Mechanics','The internal learned variables, weights and biases, that store what a model knows, counted in billions for modern LLMs. Parameter count is the headline size number, and only one of the three scaling inputs.','Models compared at 7, 70, and 400-plus billion parameters.',''),
array('PEFT','peft','Training & Mechanics','Parameter-efficient fine-tuning: the family of methods that adapt large models by training only a small fraction of weights. LoRA is its best-known member; the family is why adaptation stopped requiring frontier budgets.','Choosing a PEFT method to tune a large model on one workstation.',''),
array('Post-Training','post-training','Training & Mechanics','All tuning after pre-training that shapes behavior: instruction tuning, preference optimization, safety training. Where helpfulness and refusal policy are instilled, and where an increasing share of capability gains now comes from.','A post-training pipeline turning a raw base model into a deployable assistant.',''),
array('PPO (Proximal Policy Optimization)','ppo-proximal-policy-optimization','Training & Mechanics','The reinforcement learning algorithm classically used in RLHF, constraining each policy update to stay near the previous one for stability. The workhorse of first-generation alignment training.','PPO driving the reinforcement stage of an RLHF pipeline.','Schulman et al., OpenAI, 2017.'),
array('Pre-training','pre-training','Training & Mechanics','The initial phase of training on a massive unlabeled corpus, where a model learns language, facts, and reasoning patterns via self-supervision. The capital-intensive stage that creates the raw capability everything after refines.','A months-long run over trillions of tokens producing a base model.',''),
array('Pruning','pruning','Training & Mechanics','Removing non-essential weights or neurons from a trained network to shrink and accelerate it. Compression for deployment: much of a large network contributes little and can go.','A pruned model matching accuracy at a fraction of the size.',''),
array('QLoRA','qlora','Training & Mechanics','An extension of LoRA that quantizes the base model to 4-bit precision during tuning, pushing fine-tuning onto consumer hardware. The democratization step past LoRA: a desktop GPU became enough.','Fine-tuning a large model on a single consumer graphics card.','Dettmers et al., 2023.'),
array('Quantization','quantization','Training & Mechanics','Compressing model weights from high precision to lower precision, INT8 or INT4, to cut memory and run on weaker hardware. The trade is small accuracy loss for large efficiency gain, and it is what puts capable models on laptops.','A 4-bit quantization fitting a mid-size model into laptop memory.',''),
array('Regularization','regularization','Training & Mechanics','The family of techniques that discourage overfitting: dropout, weight decay, early stopping, data augmentation. Collectively, the discipline of making models learn structure instead of noise.','Weight decay and early stopping steadying a small-data fine-tune.',''),
array('Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Rewards (RLVR)','reinforcement-learning-with-verifiable-rewards-rlvr','Training & Mechanics','Reinforcement learning where the reward comes from an objective checker, a test suite or answer key, rather than human preference. It removed the preference bottleneck for domains with ground truth, and it is how modern reasoning models train.','Math answers and unit tests grading millions of attempts automatically.',''),
array('Reward Model','reward-model','Training & Mechanics','A model trained to score outputs by predicted human preference, used as the grader inside reinforcement learning. The scorer inside RLHF, and the component whose flaws reward hacking exploits.','A reward model ranking candidate responses during alignment training.',''),
array('RLAIF (Reinforcement Learning from AI Feedback)','rlaif-reinforcement-learning-from-ai-feedback','Training & Mechanics','An alignment method in which AI models evaluate and critique other models\' outputs, replacing much of the human feedback in the loop. It scales past human labeling capacity; Constitutional AI is its best-known form.','AI-generated preference labels standing in for human raters at scale.','Bai et al., Anthropic, 2022.'),
array('RLHF (Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback)','rlhf-reinforcement-learning-from-human-feedback','Training & Mechanics','The fine-tuning technique that uses human preference rankings to align model outputs with human intent, helpfulness, and safety. The method that turned raw language models into usable assistants, and the source of trained-in quirks like sycophancy.','Human raters\' preferences shaping a model\'s tone and judgment.','Christiano et al., 2017; applied to LLMs by OpenAI and Anthropic from 2020.'),
array('Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT)','supervised-fine-tuning-sft','Training & Mechanics','Fine-tuning on curated demonstration data, the first stage of most alignment pipelines. Demonstrations set the floor; preference optimization then shapes the ceiling.','Expert-written responses teaching format and judgment before RL.',''),
array('Tokens per Parameter','tokens-per-parameter','Training & Mechanics','The ratio guiding how much data a model of a given size should see during training. The Chinchilla finding in one number: modern runs push it far above the old defaults.','A training plan sized at tens of tokens per parameter.',''),
array('Underfitting','underfitting','Training & Mechanics','A model too simple to capture the underlying structure of its training data, performing poorly everywhere. The opposite failure to overfitting, and the cheaper one to diagnose.','A linear model flatlining on plainly non-linear data.',''),
array('Weights','weights','Training & Mechanics','The learned numerical values that determine connection strength between artificial neurons, adjusted throughout training. They are what a model is: releasing them releases the model, stealing them steals it.','Billions of weights encoding everything a model learned.',''),
array('Guardian Agent','guardian-agent','AI Security & Assurance','An AI system deployed to supervise other AI systems, monitoring their outputs and actions, enforcing policy, and intervening when a supervised agent drifts outside its mandate. The premise is that human review cannot keep pace with machine-speed activity, so a second layer of AI watches the first. The obvious question, who guards the guardian, is answered by keeping the guardian narrow, auditable, and stripped of the autonomy it polices.','A guardian agent halting a procurement agent that starts issuing purchase orders outside its authorized vendor list.','Popularized by Gartner research on agent oversight.'),
array('Autonomy Levels (Agentic AI)','agentic-autonomy-levels','Agents','A graduated scale describing how much an AI agent may decide and do without a human, running from tool-like systems that only respond, through agents that act within pre-approved boundaries, to systems that set their own subgoals. Levels turn the vague word autonomous into something a policy can bound: an organization can permit level-2 conduct and forbid level-4, then audit against the line. China\'s 2026 agent framework applies the same instinct in law with its three-tier decision-authorization model.','An enterprise policy capping customer-facing agents at supervised autonomy while allowing full autonomy in sandboxed testing.','Formalized in OECD AI Paper No. 56, The Agentic AI Landscape and its Conceptual Foundations.'),
array('Agent Hijacking','agent-hijacking','AI Security & Assurance','An attack that seizes control of an AI agent\'s behavior, typically by planting instructions in content the agent will read, a webpage, an email, a document, so the agent executes the attacker\'s task with the user\'s permissions. It is prompt injection weaponized against systems that can act, which converts a text-manipulation trick into unauthorized purchases, data exfiltration, or code execution. Defenses center on least-privilege tool access, isolating untrusted content, and human confirmation for consequential actions.','A calendar invite whose hidden text instructs an email agent to forward the inbox to an outside address.','Studied at scale in NIST CAISI red-teaming research on AI agent security.'),
array('Runtime Enforcement','runtime-enforcement','AI Security & Assurance','Controls that constrain an AI system while it is running, blocking, filtering, or rewriting non-compliant actions in real time rather than relying on pre-deployment testing alone. The shift it represents: from certifying a model once to policing its behavior continuously, which is the only posture that holds when systems adapt, use tools, and encounter inputs no test suite anticipated.','A policy engine intercepting an agent\'s outbound API call and stripping fields it is not licensed to transmit.',''),
array('The AI Efficiency Tax™','ai-efficiency-tax','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','The total operational cost of making AI output usable: not one number but five cost streams absorbed simultaneously into different budgets, none labeled as AI-related. The five components are review burden, rework cycles, output inconsistency cost, management overhead, and shadow process cost, and because each hides in a different line item, looking for the tax as a single figure misses most of it.','A team saving an hour per draft with AI while spending ninety minutes reviewing, correcting, and reconciling the output.','Coined by Stephen R. Jordan in The AI Efficiency & Process Optimization, Volume IV of The Operating Discipline for AI Library.'),
array('The AI Efficiency Gap™','ai-efficiency-gap','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','The measurable distance between what leadership expected AI to improve and what the business can actually prove AI has changed. Its signature: cycle times flat, error rates unmoved, capacity pressure unchanged, rework quietly rising, while AI usage grows steadily for months. Naming the gap is the precondition for measuring it.','A P&L showing no improvement after a year of expanding AI subscriptions.','Coined by Stephen R. Jordan in The AI Efficiency & Process Optimization, Volume IV of The Operating Discipline for AI Library.'),
array('The AI Efficiency Scorecard™','ai-efficiency-scorecard','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','A leadership instrument that evaluates each active AI use case on five performance categories to support one of four decisions: expand, refine, pause, or remove. Paired with the AI Process Fit Test, it gives leadership two independent signals pointing at the same decision.','An expand decision issued when three of five Scorecard categories clear their thresholds.','Coined by Stephen R. Jordan in The AI Efficiency & Process Optimization, Volume IV of The Operating Discipline for AI Library.'),
array('The AI ROI Formula™','ai-roi-formula','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','AI ROI equals total AI benefit minus total AI cost, divided by total AI cost, expressed as a percentage, with a complete cost denominator covering every real expense the investment generated, not just the subscription fee. It converts cycle-time, capacity, error-rate, and rework measurements into a single figure defensible under financial scrutiny.','A claimed 300% ROI collapsing to 40% once review time and rework enter the denominator.','Coined by Stephen R. Jordan in The AI Efficiency & Process Optimization, Volume IV of The Operating Discipline for AI Library.'),
array('The AI Operating System™','ai-operating-system','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','The integrated operating discipline that connects business enablement, readiness assessment, risk governance, and security into one management system, installed progressively across the nine books of The Operating Discipline for AI Library. Each book\'s frameworks sit inside it rather than standing alone.','The AI Efficiency Scorecard feeding the same quarterly cadence as the governance review.','Coined by Stephen R. Jordan in The Operating Discipline for AI Library.'),
array('Cycle Time','cycle-time','Business & Adoption','The elapsed time from the start of a unit of work to its usable completion, the first metric AI efficiency claims must survive. AI that speeds a task while lengthening the full cycle through review and rework has improved nothing measurable.','Draft time falling 60% while document turnaround stays at four days.',''),
array('Error Rate','error-rate','Business & Adoption','The share of outputs containing defects requiring correction, measured at the workflow level rather than the tool level. AI shifts where errors occur more often than it removes them.','Fewer typos, more confidently wrong figures.',''),
array('Exception Handling','exception-handling','Business & Adoption','The routing of cases that fall outside an automated or AI-assisted path to human judgment. Exception volume is the honest measure of how much a process is actually automated.','An invoice bot handling 70% of volume while the exception queue absorbs two analysts.',''),
array('Lean','lean','Business & Adoption','The waste-elimination discipline from manufacturing, applied to AI operations: AI adds capacity, Lean asks whether the underlying process deserved automating at all. Automating a wasteful process produces faster waste.','Value-stream mapping before an AI rollout removing three approval steps no one could justify.',''),
array('Decision Influence Matrix™','decision-influence-matrix','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','A four-tier impact classification for AI-influenced decisions, running Low, Moderate, High, Critical, where each tier prescribes a specific human-oversight control profile: which of the AI Decision Accountability Framework™\'s three controls are required and what is added at the higher tiers. Classification is by the decision\'s impact, not the tool\'s sophistication.','A chatbot drafting marketing copy classed Low while the same model screening loan applicants is Critical.','Coined by Stephen R. Jordan in The AI Risk & Governance Review, Volume III of The Operating Discipline for AI Library.'),
array('AI Decision Accountability Framework™','ai-decision-accountability-framework','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','The upstream control framework assigning a named human owner to every consequential AI-influenced decision, with three core controls the Decision Influence Matrix™ scales by impact tier. It exists so that "the AI decided" is never the answer to a board, regulator, acquirer, or plaintiff.','A credit denial traceable to a named reviewer, not a model version.','Introduced in Volume I and extended in Volume III of The Operating Discipline for AI Library, by Stephen R. Jordan.'),
array('AI Incident Response Framework™','ai-incident-response-framework','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','The framework defining what counts as an AI incident, who responds, and in what order: detection, containment, root-cause, notification, and corrective action, wired to regulatory clocks like the EU AI Act\'s serious-incident reporting. AI incidents differ from IT incidents because the system keeps producing confident output while wrong.','A silent model drift caught by output monitoring and triaged before customer harm.','Coined by Stephen R. Jordan in The AI Risk & Governance Review, Volume III of The Operating Discipline for AI Library.'),
array('AI Operational Risk Assessment™','ai-operational-risk-assessment','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','The scoring instrument run against each AI use case across the AI Operational Risk Categories™, producing the risk profile that drives oversight intensity, review cadence, and sign-off requirements.','A high-scoring use case pulled into quarterly management review while low scores run on spot checks.','Introduced in Volume I and extended in Volume III of The Operating Discipline for AI Library, by Stephen R. Jordan.'),
array('AI Board Reporting Package™','ai-board-reporting-package','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','The recurring eight-section board artifact supporting the oversight mandate: a structured summary, executive summary first, with drill-down detail accessible rather than attached. Built so directors can evidence Caremark-grade oversight of AI.','A one-page executive summary opening the quarterly package.','Coined by Stephen R. Jordan in The AI Risk & Governance Review, Volume III of The Operating Discipline for AI Library.'),
array('AI Governance Maturity Scale™','ai-governance-maturity-scale','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','A company-wide scoring instrument rating governance maturity across five dimensions, oversight, accountability, controls, documentation, and review cadence, each on a five-point scale from Ad Hoc to Optimized, summing to a Governance Maturity Index of 5 to 25.','A firm scoring 11 setting a twelve-month target of 18.','Coined by Stephen R. Jordan in The AI Risk & Governance Review, Volume III of The Operating Discipline for AI Library.'),
array('Standing AI Adoption Policy™','standing-ai-adoption-policy','SRJ Consulting & Services Frameworks','The always-on policy governing which AI tools and uses are approved, under what conditions, and through what request path, replacing case-by-case improvisation with a standing rule set.','An employee\'s new-tool request routed through the policy\'s approval path instead of a Slack thread.','Introduced in Volume I and extended in Volume III of The Operating Discipline for AI Library, by Stephen R. Jordan.'),
array('Three Lines of Defense','three-lines-of-defense','Safety & Governance','The governance model separating operational ownership (first line), risk and compliance oversight (second line), and independent internal audit (third line), now applied to AI systems. AI blurs the model because the same team often builds, uses, and checks the model, which is exactly the condition the three lines exist to prevent.','A data science team validating its own model, collapsing three lines into one.',''),
array('Risk Register','risk-register','Safety & Governance','The living inventory of identified risks with owner, severity, likelihood, and treatment, which AI governance frameworks extend with AI-specific entries. An unregistered AI risk is unmanaged by definition.','Shadow AI use entering the register with an owner and a remediation date.',''),
array('SR 11-7','sr-11-7','Safety & Governance','The Federal Reserve\'s 2011 supervisory guidance on model risk management, the de facto ancestor of AI governance: model inventory, independent validation, and effective challenge. Bank examiners now read AI systems through its lens, whether or not the institution calls them models.','An LLM-based underwriting assistant swept into the model inventory under SR 11-7.','Federal Reserve SR Letter 11-7, Supervisory Guidance on Model Risk Management, 2011.'),
array('Management Review','management-review','Safety & Governance','The recurring leadership evaluation of the governance system itself, required by ISO/IEC 42001 clause 9.3: whether the system is adequate, effective, and resourced. The minutes are the audit evidence that oversight actually happened.','A quarterly review adjusting audit cadence after two AI incidents.','Formalized as clause 9.3 of ISO/IEC 42001:2023.'),
array('Caremark Duty','caremark-duty','Safety & Governance','The Delaware doctrine that boards must implement and monitor a reporting system for mission-critical risks, with personal liability for conscious failure to oversee. AI\'s arrival on the mission-critical list makes it the legal floor under board AI oversight.','Board minutes documenting recurring AI risk reporting as Caremark evidence.','In re Caremark International Inc. Derivative Litigation, Delaware Court of Chancery, 1996.'),
array('Post-Market Monitoring','post-market-monitoring','Safety & Governance','The EU AI Act obligation to monitor a high-risk AI system\'s performance after deployment and feed findings back into the risk-management system. Deployment is where the obligation starts, not where it ends.','Field performance data triggering a model update and a refreshed conformity assessment.','Article 72 of the EU AI Act.'),
array('Tabletop Exercise','tabletop-exercise','Safety & Governance','A facilitated walkthrough of a simulated incident testing whether response plans, roles, and escalation paths actually work before a real event does. AI tabletops rehearse scenarios like silent drift, prompt injection, or an unannounced vendor model change.','A two-hour exercise revealing nobody knew who could shut the chatbot off.',''),
);
